('wger_1019','Side plank right','Side plank right','Starting position:

Lie down on your side, with your bottom elbow at a right angle, arm sticking out. Lift your pelvis off the floor by lifting your bottom shoulder up, keeping the forearm on the floor; your head, pelvis, and feet should be in a straight line.

Steps:

Hold this position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1019','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1020','Pistol squats right','Pistol squats right','Stand on one leg, with your other leg straight and slightly forward.
Bend one knee slowly, descending into a squat and keeping your back and your other leg straight.
Slowly raise yourself from the squat, straightening the bent knee and keeping the other leg straight.
Repeat.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','hamstrings','calves','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1020','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1021','Calf raises, right leg','Calf raises, right leg','Stand on the floor or on the edge of a step to increase the range of movement.
Raise one foot.
Lift your heel until you''re standing on your toes.
(variable) Stay in this position for three seconds
Slowly lower your foot until you almost touch the ground with your heel - don''t slam your foot!','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Calves',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1021','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1022','Single Arm Plank to Row','Single Arm Plank to Row','Start position as row, extend to plank and back. Finish with row and repeat','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Back','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1022/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1022','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1027','Elevated prayer stretch','Elevated prayer stretch','Starting position:
Kneel in front of a bench, far enough so that your torso can fit between your knees and the bench. With your back straight, place your elbows on the bench, with palms together, hands pointing up.
Steps:

On exhale, stretch your chest down toward the floor without moving your lower back. At the same time, bring your hands toward your shoulders, keeping palms together and elbows on the bench.
Hold for a few seconds.
On inhale, relax your back to return to the starting position.

Repeat.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1027','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1028','Quadruped thoracic rotation left','Quadruped thoracic rotation left','Starting position:
Start kneeling on all fours, knees shoulder-width apart. Place your left hand behind your head while keeping your right hand outstretched and touching the floor.
Steps:

On inhale, move your left elbow toward your right hand, keeping your left hand behind your head.
On exhale, move your left elbow to point up toward the ceiling.
Repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1028','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1029','Quadruped thoracic rotation right','Quadruped thoracic rotation right','Starting position:

Start kneeling on all fours, knees shoulder-width apart. Place your right hand behind your head while keeping your left hand outstretched and touching the floor.

Steps:

On inhale, move your right elbow toward your left hand, keeping your right hand behind your head.
On exhale, move your right elbow to point up toward the ceiling.
Repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1029','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1080','Hindu Pushups','Hindu Pushups','Exercise to strengthen the shoulders and pectorals. Its name is due to the fact that it begins in the Yoga position "Dog Facing Down", passing to "Cobra" but without resting the legs or torso on the ground to finally end with a normal flexion. The exercise can also be performed backwards (back to the starting position). As a variation, after doing the push-up, the hip can be raised to return to downward facing dog.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1080/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1080','CC-BY-SA 4','Imobard','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1081','Shoulder dislocates','Shoulder dislocates','Starting position:
Stand up with your back straight and a resistance band, towel, or broomstick handle in hand. With your hands straight in front of your body and the band between your hands, push your hands apart to both be at around 45 degrees from your body, thumbs facing down. If using a towel or broomstick handle instead, grab it with an overhand grip.
Steps:

Keeping your arms outstretched, rotate at the shoulders to bring your arms overhead and then down toward your glutes.
Rotate at the shoulders in the opposite direction — overhead and then toward your groin.
Repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1081','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1082','Bent over row to external rotation','Bent over row to external rotation','Starting position:
Stand behind a chair or in front of a table. Bend at the waist to put your forehead on the chair''s headrest or table, keeping your back straight. Your arms should be hanging straight down, pointed at the floor.
Steps:

Bring your elbows up to shoulder height. Your forearms should be pointing down, perpendicular to your biceps. Your biceps should be at the same height as your back and perpendicular to your spine.
Hold for a bit.
Rotate at your elbows to bring your hands as far up as you can.
Hold for a bit.
Rotate at your elbows back to the previous position.
Bring your arms down to the original position.
Repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1082','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1083','YWTs','YWTs','Starting position:
Lie down, preferably on a mat. Stretch your arms above your head in a "Y" position (arms pointing up diagonally at around 45 degrees). Your thumbs should be pointing up.
Steps:

With arms in the Y position, lift your chest slightly from the ground, creating a pull tension in your arms upward.
Hold this position for several seconds (15–30 is ideal).
Keeping your chest up, bend at your elbows to move from a Y position to a "W" position, with arms bent at the elbows and maintaining the upward tension.
Hold for around as long as with the Y position.
Still with your chest up, move to a "T" position, straightening your arms out to the side to be perpendicular to your body.
Hold for around as long as you held the W position.
Move from the T position to the W position, then from the W position to the Y position.
Repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1083','CC-BY-SA 4','tinman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1084','Dumbbell Floor Press','Dumbbell Floor Press','Grab your dumbbells and lay flat on your back with your knees bent and your feet flat on the ground (use a bench if you have one). Press the weights up, locking out your elbows (A). Lower them slowly until your upper arms are resting on the floor (B) close to your body. Pause here before explosively pressing back up. Squeeze your chest hard and repeat.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','biceps','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1084/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1084','CC-BY-SA 4','admin','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1086','Close-grip Press-ups','Close-grip Press-ups','Drop into a strong plank position, bringing your hands close together until they''re almost touching. (picture 1)Bend your elbows to slowly bring your chest to the floor (picture 2). Keep your elbows close to your body as you push back up explosively. Repeat. Ensure you take your time lowering on each rep, keeping your form sharp.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','chest','shoulders','biceps','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1086/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1086','CC-BY-SA 4','philip','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1087','Dumbbell Hang Power Cleans','Dumbbell Hang Power Cleans','On your feet, stand tall with your dumbbells, holding them at your sides. Hinge at the hips to lower them to your knees (picture 1). Stand back up with a slight jump, using the momentum to pull the dumbbells up on to your shoulders (picture 2). Stand up straight, then lower under control to your sides and repeat. Keep this fast and explosive; if your heart rate doesn’t hit the roof, you’re doing them wrong.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','calves','quads']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1087/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1087','CC-BY-SA 4','philip','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1088','Dumbbell sumo deadlift','Dumbbell sumo deadlift','Lower your dumbbell to the ground between your legs. Assume a wide stance and with a straight back squat down. With the dumbbell standing upright, grip it by the top of the ‘head’ (picture 1).Keeping your chest up and core braced, push the floor away, driving back upwards to a standing position (picture 2). Repeat. If you can easily achieve 20-30 reps, use two dumbbells.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1088/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1088','CC-BY-SA 4','philip','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1089','Medicine ball twist','Medicine ball twist','In a seated position, the torso is rotated from side to side without forcing, approaching the knees and making the ball touch the ground from time to time','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1089/0.jpeg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1089','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
