('wger_1131','Cable glute extension','Cable glute extension','This exercise lets you work the upper, or larger, part of the glutes. For that reason, it should never be missing from your routine of isolated exercises for training the glutes.
Stand in front of a cable machine and locate the low pulley. Then attach the ankle strap to work on the low pulley. As for your posture, you should stay upright at all times. Pay special attention to your back to keep it straight and avoid injury.
It is advisable to hold on to the machine for better balance. With the leg that is holding the weight of the cable, perform a slow stretch backward without bending the knee.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1131/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1131','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1132','Machine glute extension','Machine glute extension','A GHD hip extension is one of the best exercises for the glutes. While the exercise mainly targets the glutes, it is also excellent for the lower back, the calves and the hamstrings.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1132','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1136','Neutral-grip chest pulldown','Neutral-grip chest pulldown','The lat pulldown is an important exercise for strengthening the back and improving posture, which can contribute to a healthier life. To perform this exercise correctly and avoid injury, it is important to follow a few key steps:

Position yourself in front of the cable machine with your knees slightly bent and your feet on the floor.

Grip the cable handle with your palms facing each other and your hands shoulder-width apart.

Pull the handle down until it touches or comes close to your chest, holding the position for one or two seconds.

Slowly raise the handle back to the starting position, making sure to keep your arms and hands straight and your back straight throughout the movement.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1136/0.PNG',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1136','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1137','High-pulley pullover','High-pulley pullover','Stand facing the machine, feet slightly apart, gripping the bar with an overhand grip, arms extended, hands shoulder-width apart.

Keeping your back fixed and your abdominal muscles contracted, inhale and bring the bar down to your thighs while keeping your arms extended (or your elbows slightly bent).
Exhale at the end of the movement.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1137/0.PNG',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1137','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1138','Incline bench pulldown','Incline bench pulldown','Lying face down on the incline bench facing the cable machine, perform the pulldown.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1138/0.PNG',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1138','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1141','Arabesque','Arabesque','Take all your weight onto one leg and you''re going to maintain that position, keeping your hips and pelvis level the whole time. With your back in a neutral position you want to tilt yourself forward kicking your leg back up and then slowly with your glutes bring yourself back up to neutral.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1141/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1141','CC-BY-SA 4','cleen','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
