('wger_1188','Side bend','Side bend','With a weight in one hand, extend that arm down and bend the other arm, resting your hand on your head. Now move the hand holding the weight by rotating your torso up and down.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1188/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1188','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1192','Alternating Biceps Curls With Dumbbell','Alternating Biceps Curls With Dumbbell','Hold two dumbbells, the arms are streched, the hands are on your
side, the palms face inwards. Bend one arm at a time and bring the weight with a
fast movement up. At the same time, rotate your arms by 90 degrees at
the very beginning of the movement. At the highest point, rotate a
little the weights further outwards. Without a pause, bring the arm back down, slowly, and do the same with the other arm.

Don''t allow your body to swing during the exercise, all work is done
by the biceps, which are the only mucles that should move (pay attention
to the elbows).','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms','alternating',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1192/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1192','CC-BY-SA 4','Franpol','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1193','Russian Twist','Russian Twist','Hold a dumbbell, barbell weight or something else that is heavy with both hands, but make sure it is not too heavy and you are able to keep in form.
Lean back to a 45-degree angle from the floor. For an extra challenge, lift your feet off the floor.
Rotate your arms to one side to the same level as your chest, touch the floor for a little extra challenge, and then do the same to the other side. When you''re back in your original position after doing both sides it will count as 1 rep.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1193/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1193','CC-BY-SA 4','lion','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1194','Pallof Press','Pallof Press','The Pallof press is an anti-rotation exercise that trains the larger and smaller muscles around the spine to resist rotation.

Stand parallel to the cable machine or to the anchor point to the
resistance band and clasp with the handle or band with both hands.
Make sure your torso is front on and bring your hands to the center of your chest and slowly press out.
Slowly return your hands to the chest and repeat.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','CORE','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes','core','chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1194/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1194','CC-BY-SA 4','prevail90','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1195','Side Slides + Squats','Side Slides + Squats','With feet a little wider than shoulder-width apart and staying low to mimic a defensive position, you should step with their lead leg and push off with their plant leg.
After three slides, rotate your body for 180 degree on the guiding (/outer) leg and do a squat. Continue.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','calves','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1195','CC-BY-SA 4','Insight','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
