('wger_1205','Wrist curl, dumbbells','Wrist curl, dumbbells','Sitting on a bench, grab the dumbbell with your palms facing up
and your hands shoulder-width apart. Rest your forearms on your thighs
and allow your wrists to hang over your knees.
Perform the movement by
curling your palms and wrists towards your face.
(optional/variable) Pause at the top.
Slowly return to the starting position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1205','CC-BY-SA 4','wakanda90','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1207','Scorpion Kick','Scorpion Kick','Get into the push-up position with your shoulders directly above your hands and your feet hip-width apart.

Make sure that your body forms a straight line from your head to your heels.

Now pull your right knee towards your chest. While keeping your knee bent, lift your right leg as high as possible with your lower right leg pointing straight up.

Now rotate your hips so that your right foot swings over your left leg.

Continue to rotate and move your right foot towards the floor until you are forced to roll onto the outside of your left standing foot. Make sure that you do not rotate your upper body.

Now return to the starting position and repeat the exercise with your left leg.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1207','CC-BY-SA 4','lxmx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1208','Prisoner Squat','Prisoner Squat','Stand upright with your chest slightly raised, your feet hip-width apart and your toes pointing straight ahead.
Bring your hands to the back of your head with your fingers slightly interlaced and your elbows pointing to the side. Push your hips back and bend your knees, keeping your upper body as upright as possible. 
Push your knees outwards, they must never point towards each other. If your upper body moves slightly forward, make sure that it does not bend. Always keep your elbows level with your ears by tensing the muscles between your shoulder blades. If you are flexible enough, you can sink down until your buttocks touch your calves.
However, make sure that you do not bend your spine. 
Before this happens, reverse the movement and use your heels and glutes to push yourself upwards with so much momentum that your feet lift off briefly and you do a little hop. 
If necessary, correct the position of your feet, arms and upper body before you move on to the next repetition.
Translated with www.DeepL.com/Translator (free version)','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1208','CC-BY-SA 4','lxmx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1209','Shoulder width three-point push-up','Shoulder width three-point push-up','Get into a push-up position with your shoulders directly above your hands and your feet hip-width apart. Draw your belly button in towards your spine and tighten your abdominal muscles. Lift your left foot about five centimetres off the floor. Point your toes straight down. Do not move your hips. Your body forms a straight line from your head to your heels throughout the exercise. Now bend your elbows, lower your chest to the floor and push yourself back up. Repeat the exercise on the other side.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1209','CC-BY-SA 4','lxmx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1210','Skydiver with arms in T-position','Skydiver with arms in T-position','Lie on your stomach with your legs more than shoulder-width apart and your feet up. Your arms are stretched out to the side and form a T with your upper body, your palms are on the floor. Now raise your upper body, arms and legs as high as you can while keeping your body under tension. Turn your thumbs towards the ceiling and pull your shoulder blades together. While keeping your upper body and all limbs in the air, bring your legs together and then spread them again, keeping them constantly in the air. For the remaining repetitions, only move your legs open and closed.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1210','CC-BY-SA 4','lxmx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1214','Front lever tuck','Front lever tuck','The muscles involved in the Front Lever, most subjected to stress, are mainly the extensors such as: the latissimus dorsi, the teres major, the posterior deltoid and the long head of the biceps.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','lats','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1214','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1215','Reverse Snow Angel','Reverse Snow Angel','Lay flat on your stomach with your arms extended in front of you on the ground as your legs are lying flat. Lift both your arms and move them to your side slowly. Then, move them back.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','hamstrings','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1215','CC-BY-SA 4','mike6426','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1216','Recruitment Pulls','Recruitment Pulls','Find a few specific edge sizes on a hangboard, get fixed underneath them with the board overhead, and pull with max effort, 1 arm at a time, for 3-5 seconds. When positioning for this get set up with a large elbow angle (120-150 degrees) and not in full extension.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1216','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1217','Finger Pushup','Finger Pushup','Hand Positioning:

Start in a plank position with your hands directly beneath your shoulders.
Spread your fingers wide apart, placing them firmly on the ground.

Finger Placement:

Gradually lift your palms off the ground, shifting the weight onto your fingers.
Focus on distributing the load evenly across your fingertips and thumbs.

Body Alignment:

Maintain a straight line from head to heels to engage your core.
Keep your body in a controlled and stable position throughout the exercise.

Lowering Phase:

Slowly bend your elbows, lowering your chest towards the ground.
Ensure controlled movement, maintaining stability on your fingertips.

Pushing Up:

Press through your fingertips to straighten your arms, returning to the starting position.
Emphasize the engagement of your fingers and thumbs throughout the push-up.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1217/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1217','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1218','knee push-ups','knee push-ups','Start by kneeling on the floor, keeping your knees together. Place your hands on the floor in front of you, slightly wider than shoulder-width apart.
Make sure your body forms a straight line from head to knees. Hands should be positioned below shoulders.
Lower your torso towards the ground, bending your elbows while keeping your trunk stable. Keep your knees in contact with the floor.
Push through your hands to return to the starting position. Be sure to maintain contraction of chest, shoulder and arm muscles at the top of the movement.
Perform the desired number of repetitions, controlling the movement and maintaining good form.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1218','CC-BY-SA 4','PaukOne','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1219','Australian pull-ups','Australian pull-ups','Lie down under a high bar or suspension bar, positioned at an appropriate height.
Position yourself on your back under the bar, gripping the bar with a supinated grip (palms facing you).
Adjust your position so that your body is aligned straight from head to toe. Arms should be fully extended, shoulders stabilized, and legs aligned with the rest of the body.
Bend your elbows and pull your chest towards the bar, contracting your back muscles. Imagine you''re trying to bring your shoulder blades together.
Hold the contraction at the top of the movement for a moment to maximize muscle activation.
Slowly return to the starting position, extending your elbows.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1219','CC-BY-SA 4','PaukOne','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1223','Claps over the head','Claps over the head','Stand with your feet shoulder width apart. Raise your arms and clap over your head','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1223/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1223','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1224','Dumbbell drag curls','Dumbbell drag curls','Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your palms facing forward. Pull your elbows back and lift the dumbbells to your chest height. Slowly lower the dumbbell and repeat the exercise.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1224','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1225','Dumbbell wide bicep curls','Dumbbell wide bicep curls','Hold a dumbbell in each hand with your hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart and palms facing forward.
Bend your elbows and lift the dumbbells to your shoulders. Slowly return and repeat.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1225/0.gif',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1225','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1226','Dumbbell bicep curl to press','Dumbbell bicep curl to press','Bend your elbows and lift the dumbbells to your shoulders.
Push the dumbbells over your head while rotating your arms to make your palms face forward. Reverse it to lower down. Repeat the exercise.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1226/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1226','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1227','Dumbbell rear delt row','Dumbbell rear delt row','Hold a dumbbell in each hand. Bend at your hips to make your back almost parallel to the floor. Let your arms hang down. Keep your arms in line with your shoulders. bend and lift your elbows out to the sides until your upper arms are parallel to the floor. Slowly return and repeat','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1227/0.gif',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1227','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1228','Dumbbell close grip bench press','Dumbbell close grip bench press','Lie down with your back on a flat bench. Hold a dumbbell in each hand. Raise your arms towards the ceiling with your palms facing each other and dumbbells pressed together.
Slowly lower the dumbbells to your chest, then slowly push them back. Repeat the exercise.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1228','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1230','Triceps stretch left','Triceps stretch left','Put your left hand on your back, use your right hand to grab your left elbow and gently pull it. Hold this position for a few seconds.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1230/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1230','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1231','Triceps stretch right','Triceps stretch right','Put your right hand on your back, use your left hand to grab your right elbow and gently pull it. Hold this position for a few seconds.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1231/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1231','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1232','Standing biceps stretch left','Standing biceps stretch left','Stand with your left arm close to a wall. Extend your left arm and put your left hand on the wall, then gently turn your body to the right.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1232/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1232','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1233','Standing biceps stretch right','Standing biceps stretch right','Stand with your right arm close to a wall. Extend your right arm and put your right hand on the wall, then gently turn your body to the left.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1233/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1233','CC-BY-SA 4','Lynn_McIntyre','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1234','Dumbbell Single-leg Hip Thrust','Dumbbell Single-leg Hip Thrust','The single-leg hip thrust is performed by placing your upper back on a weight bench, raising one leg, and extending the hip of the other leg to achieve an isolated contraction of the glute.
By working each side separately, you can fully isolate your glutes unilaterally, providing maximal training stimulus.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings','quads']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1234','CC-BY-SA 4','carlos3c','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1238','Frog stand','Frog stand','Starting position:
Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart and your toes pointing forward, facing a wall or bench for support if needed.
Bend your knees into a squat position.
Place your hands on the ground in front of you, shoulder-width apart, with your fingers spread wide.
Make sure your elbows are under your shoulders and your body forms a straight line from your head to your heels.
Upward phase:
Push with your feet and hands to lift your body off the ground.
Straighten your legs and arms, keeping your body aligned.
Engage your core and glutes to maintain the position.
If needed, rest your knees on the wall or bench for assistance.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1238','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1239','Standing Calf Stretch','Standing Calf Stretch','This stretch targets the gastrocnemius (the chief muscle of the calf of the leg, which flexes the knee and foot). It is easy to perform anywhere. All you need is a wall or a chair.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1239/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1239','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_124','Braced Squat','Braced Squat','Stand with feet slightly wider than shoulder-width apart, while standing as tall as you can.

Grab a weight plate and hold it out in front of your body with arms straight out. Keep your core tight and stand with a natural arch in your back.

Now, push hips back and bend knees down into a squat as far as you can. Hold for a few moments and bring yourself back up to the starting position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','124','CC-BY-SA 4','sevae','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1240','Standing Soleus Stretch','Standing Soleus Stretch','This stretch targets the Soleus part of your calf. It may be performed with a wall or chair.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1240','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1241','Exercise Band Dorsiflexion','Exercise Band Dorsiflexion','This exercise uses an exercise band. It targets the Soleus and Tibialis anterior.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1241','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1242','Exercise Band Plantarflexion','Exercise Band Plantarflexion','Banded plantarflexion is a great way to bridge the gap between plantarflexion range of motion and the more strenuous calf raises in weight bearing. This can help strengthen the calf muscles, load the Achilles tendon, and improve plantarflexion range of motion.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1242','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1243','Double Leg Calf Raise','Double Leg Calf Raise','The double leg heel raise is important to strengthen and create control and stability around the ankle and knee, and provide balance and control for the hip and pelvis.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs','bilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1243/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1243','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1244','Yoga exercise: Cow-cat','Yoga exercise: Cow-cat','First get into the four-footed stance. The hands are underneath the shoulders. The fingers are fanned out wide and ensure a stable stance. It is best to rest your front body weight on your thumbs and index fingers. Now place your legs hip-width apart on the yoga mat. Your thighs should be vertically below your hips. Make sure that your weight is evenly distributed between your hands and knees. Your head is an extension of your spine and you are looking down at your mat. Your back is in a neutral position. Breathe in deeply and start with the cat. With the next exhalation, round your back vertebra by vertebra. Try to pull yourself as far as possible towards the ceiling. Pull your head towards your chest and tilt your pelvis. Now inhale deeply and move into the opposite position, cow pose. Bend your back down, pull your shoulders back slightly and lift your head as far as is comfortable for you. Your gaze is directed upwards. Breathe out consciously and switch back to the cat. With the next exhalation, switch back to cow. Repeat the exercise a few times and make sure that you are in the flow.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1244','CC-BY-SA 4','damnlost','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1245','Front Lever','Front Lever','The front lever is a figure where the body is kept in a horizontal position parallel to the floor.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1245','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1246','TRX roll out','TRX roll out','Hold the handles in your hands, extend your arms and keep them parallel at chest height. The movement you need to perform is to open your arms in line with your shoulders while leaning your body forward. Try not to extend your shoulders beyond 90°, and keep your abdominal muscles and glutes contracted. Muscles involved: transverse abdominis, rectus abdominis and spinal erectors.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1246','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1248','Ice cream maker','Ice cream maker','From the final phase of a pull-up, we push ourselves back with our shoulders until we reach the front lever position. From there, we pull ourselves back up to the starting position.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1248','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1252','Front lever pull-up','Front lever pull-up','in the front lever position, with legs extended or easier if collected, pull by bringing the chest closer to the bar.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK','CORE','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats','core','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1252','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1259','TRX Obliques','TRX Obliques','Place your feet in the stirrups and assume a high plank with your hands directly beneath your shoulders.
Pull your knees to your right elbow, then push them back out and to the centre.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['core','shoulders','chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1259','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1260','TRX hammer curl','TRX hammer curl','Place the grips as if they were a continuation of the straps. We will position our arms stretched forward and our body leaning back, completely straight. The biceps muscles will activate as you bend your elbows to bring your body towards the straps. The contraction movement will end with a slight outward movement of the hands, due to the grip we are using.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1260','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1261','TRX gorilla biceps curl','TRX gorilla biceps curl','We''ll stand facing the TRX straps and grab them with our fists facing each other, facing forward, with our arms fully extended at about shoulder-width apart. We''ll keep our body straight, backward, as in the previous exercises, since we''ll be lifting our body toward the TRX straps by activating our biceps. Our body will be straight, with our feet flat on the floor. This time, we''ll place our arms open to the sides and at chest height. The movement we''ll perform is a contraction toward our chest. To achieve this, we''ll bend our elbows so that, by activating our biceps, we can pull our body toward the straps.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1261','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1262','Trx Single Arm Bicep Curl','Trx Single Arm Bicep Curl','Step 1: Stand comfortably and grasp the handles of the suspension system. Step 2: Lean back resting your weight on one arm, keepng the spine neutral. Step 3: Slowly curl to pull your body weight to the up position. Supinate the arm and squeeze as you approach the end position. Step 4: Lower yourself back down and repeat.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1262','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1263','Back bridge','Back bridge','Lie on the floor with your back resting on the floor and your legs bent, feet flat on the floor, leaving about 20 cm between your feet and your buttocks. Your hands remain flat on the floor, pressed against your ears, with your fingers pointing toward your toes. Your elbows are bent and pointing toward the ceiling. This is the starting position. Now push your hips as high as you can, raising your body off the floor, and continue pushing through your hands, extending your elbows and knees, until your back is fully arched (lumbar bridge). Your head also comes off the floor and should be level with your elbows, looking back. This is the final position. The descent should be slow and controlled. Your spine should be in a convex curve. It''s not good to lift your back off the floor; it should remain straight. It should be well rounded. You''ll also notice a feeling of increased oxygenation in your back. After lifting off the floor, your hips should be very high, even above the level of your head. Your arms and legs should remain straight. It seems easy, but it requires a good level of flexibility. Breathing should be deep. This posture stretches the rib cage and puts pressure on the diaphragm. If the posture is performed correctly, breathing will be perfect. Never hold your breath during the exercise.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','hamstrings','calves','lats','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1263','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1266','TRX Tricep Extension','TRX Tricep Extension','Attach the TRX or other suspension system overhead, having the handles hanging at chest level or slightly lower. Experiment to see what height allows you to set up in the best way.
Stand in front of the handles and grab them with your palms facing down.
Engage your abs, squeeze your glutes, take a breath and lean forward, lifting your heels off the floor. Keep your elbows straight.
Take another breath and lower yourself slowly by bending your elbows.
Go down until your elbows are at a 90-degree angle (to the point where your wrists are above your elbows). Hold the position for a moment.
Extend your arms by engaging your triceps and bring yourself to the starting position as you exhale.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1266','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1269','TRX dips','TRX dips','Start with the hands on the suspension trainer and feet on the ground.
Your hands should be under your shoulders with the feet slightly in front.
Lower yourself by bringing the hips between the handles and flexing the elbows.
Extend the elbows to come back to the starting position and repeat.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1269','CC-BY-SA 4','cynomops','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1270','Low Pulley Cable Fly','Low Pulley Cable Fly','Adjust the cable machine: Set the pulley to the lowest setting possible.
Choose your handles: You can use neutral grip handles (palms facing each other) or straight handles depending on your preference. Neutral grip might be easier on your wrists.
Stand with proper form: Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent, and core engaged. Maintain a slight arch in your lower back throughout the exercise.
Grip the handles: Grab the handles with your chosen grip and step back a small step or two until there''s slight tension on the cables.
Initiate the movement: Keep your elbows slightly bent throughout the exercise. Imagine you''re giving someone a big hug. Squeeze your chest muscles as you bring your hands together in front of your chest.
Control the movement: Focus on squeezing your chest muscles rather than using your arms to pull the handles.
Peak contraction: Briefly hold the squeeze at the top of the movement with your hands together at chest level.
Return slowly: Slowly release the tension and return the handles back down to the starting position with your arms slightly extended but not locked out.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1270','CC-BY-SA 4','FEFFO','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1273','Pullover','Pullover','Doubling as a back and chest exercise, the Dumbbell Pullover can train both your pecs and lats.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['chest','lats']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1273','CC-BY-SA 4','3leh','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1274','Sitting Calf Stretch (Dorsiflexion)','Sitting Calf Stretch (Dorsiflexion)','This is a light stretch for the calf that is great for rehab.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1274/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1274','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1275','Plantarflexion Stretch with Band','Plantarflexion Stretch with Band','This stretch is for the ankles, as well as Tibialis anterior.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1275/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1275','CC-BY-SA 4','erikocobra','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1280','Biceps Close Grip Pull Down','Biceps Close Grip Pull Down','On a lat pull down machine, hold the bar keeping your hands relatively close. Use an underhand grip (I.E.: the back of your hand must be facing the machine). Then pull down the bar in a straight line towards the ground. Make sure your biceps are the main drivers of the motion. You will probably feel your shoulders and lats working, but make sure your biceps are working more.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','shoulders','lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1280','CC-BY-SA 4','daniel.escada','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1282','Isometria trazioni impugnatura inversa','Isometria trazioni impugnatura inversa','Trazioni in isometria con impugnatura inversa','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1282','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1283','Incline Chest-Supported Dumbbell Row','Incline Chest-Supported Dumbbell Row','Set up an adjustable bench at a 45-degree angle.
Lay on your stomach with your head hanging just above the edge of the bench.
Grab a dumbbell in each hand and set up with a good posture – core and lats engaged and shoulders neutral.
Row the dumbbells toward the top of the stomach and squeeze the back at the top of the rep.
Finally, lower the dumbbells back to the starting position and repeat until all reps are completed.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1283/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1283','CC-BY-SA 4','carlos3c','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1284','Pseudo Planche Push-up','Pseudo Planche Push-up','You should have the shoulder line in front of your wrists an perform a push-up, maintaining the shoulder in the same position','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1284','CC-BY-SA 4','vdrb','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1285','Talons fesses','Talons fesses','Touch your heels to your buttocks, while remaining static or moving','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves','hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1285/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1285','CC-BY-SA 4','painDpice','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1286','Dynamic Planche','Dynamic Planche','Start in a plank position, with your hands directly under your shoulders and your feet hip-width apart.
Engage your core to keep your body in a straight line from head to toe.
From this position, bend your knees slightly and jump with both feet inward, bringing them as close to your core as possible
As soon as your feet touch the ground, push off forcefully to jump again and return to the starting plank position.
Continue repeating this jumping motion, maintaining control and core stability throughout the exercise.
Make sure to keep your breathing steady while jumping, breathing deeply and controlling your breathing.
Keep your gaze fixed on the ground to maintain proper spinal alignment.
Repeat the jumps for the desired length of time or the number of repetitions recommended for your workout program.
To finish the exercise, rest by releasing the plank position, then stretch if necessary to loosen your muscles.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1286','CC-BY-SA 4','painDpice','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1287','Reach ups','Reach ups','To perform this exercise, lie on your back with your arms extended overhead. Then, contract your abdominals and lift your torso off the floor while reaching your arms toward the ceiling to "reach" as high as possible. Slowly return to the starting position, controlling the movement. Reach ups strengthen the abdominal muscles and improve the flexibility of the spine. They can be incorporated into a variety of training routines to work on core strength and stability.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1287','CC-BY-SA 4','painDpice','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1288','Dynamic side plank','Dynamic side plank','The dynamic side plank involves positioning yourself on your side, supported on one elbow and the side of your foot, then dipping your hips up and down while keeping your body in a straight line.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1288','CC-BY-SA 4','painDpice','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1289','Seated Dumbbell Curls','Seated Dumbbell Curls','Seated Dumbbell Curls are an effective bicep workout that isolates the muscles by stabilizing the upper body, reducing momentum that can detract from the exercise’s effectiveness. This exercise is performed sitting down with a dumbbell in each hand, focusing on controlled movement to maximize engagement of the bicep muscles.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1289','CC-BY-SA 4','sTiKyt','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_129','Chest Press','Chest Press','Adjust the seat height so that the grips are parallel to your chest.
Use your legs to push the foot forward pedal.
Bring the handles to the start position.
Keep your back in contact with the back pad, press outwards.
Press the handles away from your chest and exhale.
Allow the handles to come in gently until they reach your chest.
Allow the handles to return to your chest as you inhale.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_129/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','129','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1290','Reverse Grip Barbell Curls','Reverse Grip Barbell Curls','Hold the barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing down) approximately shoulder-width apart. Ensure your back is straight, shoulders slightly pulled back, and arms fully extended.
Curl the barbell upwards towards your chest in a controlled motion, keeping your elbows close to your body. The motion should be smooth without any swinging or momentum use.
Once the barbell is at chest level, pause briefly to maximize contraction in the biceps and forearms.
Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position with a controlled movement, fully extending your arms.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1290/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1290','CC-BY-SA 4','sTiKyt','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1292','Reverse-grip pull-ups','Reverse-grip pull-ups','Pull-ups on the bar with your thumbs pointing outward.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1292','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1293','One armed push-ups','One armed push-ups','Perform push-ups with one hand, alternating the sides','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS','SHOULDERS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps','shoulders','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1293','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1294','Single-leg hamstring curl','Single-leg hamstring curl','Specifically, the muscles involved are: biceps femoris, semimembranosus and semitendinosus.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1294','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1296','Low-Cable Cross-Over - NB','Low-Cable Cross-Over - NB','The low-cable cross-over is an isolation movement that uses a cable stack to target the upper portion of the pectoral muscles. It is common in upper-body and chest-focused muscle-building workouts, often in combination with presses or flyes from other angles to target all portions of the chest.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1296/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1296','CC-BY-SA 4','JackSparrow','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1298','High-Cable Cross Tricep Extention - NB','High-Cable Cross Tricep Extention - NB','The high-cable cross tricep extension is an isolation exercise for targeting the triceps,
particularly the long head. It utilizes cables and handles grasped with opposite hands, allowing for a unique pressing motion that can be effective for building tricep strength. Unlike exercises that use a straight bar or rope, this variation can be more comfortable on your wrists and elbows','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1298/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1298','CC-BY-SA 4','JackSparrow','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1302','JM Press','JM Press','The JM press keeps your shoulders stationary, relying on the elbow flexion and extension to move the weight using your triceps strength. That means you get all the benefits of the best triceps-strengthening exercises without overtaxing that delicate shoulder joint. Classic win-win!','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','biceps','chest']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1302','CC-BY-SA 4','Epiphany8424','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1303','Helms Row','Helms Row','Setup: Place your chest on the end of a bench, using a towel or anything soft to keep your chest protected. You want your chest to be in contact with the bench around the nipple line. Your back should be almost parallel to the floor
Execution: When you’re starting the exercise, focus on pulling your elbows back until you feel maximum tightness in the lats.
If you want to get some trap activation with the exercise, relax your shoulder blades when the weights are hanging down and then retract them as you start the rep.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1303','CC-BY-SA 4','carlos3c','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1304','Meadows Row','Meadows Row','The Meadows row is a unilateral row performed with a landmine setup, overhand grip, and staggered stance. Lean your torso forward and grip the barbell. Rest the other forearm on the forward leg. Start this movement by driving the elbow behind you while retracting the shoulder-blade. Keep the working shoulder down. Pull toward your back hip until the elbow is level with your torso.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps','core']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1304','CC-BY-SA 4','carlos3c','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1307','Front Plank','Front Plank','The plank is a bodyweight exercise. As a multi-functional movement, the plank not only targets your abdominal muscles but also the spine and hip. Plank strengthens and tightens your entire body, improves your posture and balance, reduces body fat, and can help boost your metabolism.
Exercises such as the “plank pose” help strengthen the stamina of stabilizing abdominal muscles. It can also help relieve back pain associated with a weakening of the function of the stabilizing muscles of the body.
Planks are a versatile exercise that targets many of the most important muscle groups in the body, so they can be applied by anyone to improve endurance and overall body strength.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','CHEST','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['core','chest','quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1307','CC-BY-SA 4','hektkaso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1312','Bodyweight Squat HD','Bodyweight Squat HD','Squat is a type of bodyweight exercise. It is one of the most popular exercises for strength and muscle growth. Squat is particularly effective for focusing on the muscles of the leg and hips.
Squat are an easy exercise for beginners to do. It can help strengthen leg muscles, tighten hip muscles and burn calories to lose weight.
It tightens the butt and legs. Squats are very effective for firming and strengthening your legs by acting on the gluteus,hip flexors, quadriceps, hamstrings and inner thigh muscles. Also, bodyweight squats can help shape your glutes and butt.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['quads','calves','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1312','CC-BY-SA 4','admin','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1314','Jumping Jack HD','Jumping Jack HD','Jumping jack are a plyometric exercise. Plyometrics are explosive aerobic moves that increase speed, quickness, and power and they work your whole body.
Jumping jack target the arm, shoulder, abdominal muscles, hip muscles and hip flexors and also work on the thighs, knee tendons and quadriceps.
Jumps are beneficial to your health because they combine cardiovascular conditioning with strength work. Since jumps elevate your heart rate, they can also improve your cardiovascular fitness.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1314','CC-BY-SA 4','hektkaso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1318','High Knee Skips HD','High Knee Skips HD','You can use this exercise both as a dynamic warm-up before training and add it to your cardio training routine to burn fat.
High knee skips are a plyometric exercise. Plyometrics are explosive aerobic moves that increase speed, quickness, and power and they work your whole body.
High knee skips target the oblique, leg muscles, hip muscles and hip flexors and also work on the thighs, knee tendons, quadriceps and shoulders.
Jumps are beneficial to your health because they combine cardiovascular conditioning with strength work. Since jumps elevate your heart rate, they can also improve your cardiovascular fitness.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','ARMS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['core','biceps','glutes','quads','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1318','CC-BY-SA 4','hektkaso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_132','Burpees','Burpees','Jump, lay down on your chest, do a pushup then jump, repeat','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','132','CC-BY-SA 4','er0355','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1320','Bench Dips On Floor HD','Bench Dips On Floor HD','Triceps dips on floor are a compound exercise as they worked multiple muscle groups simultaneously. Although this bodyweight exercise mainly targets the triceps, it also hits your chest and front of your shoulder.
Triceps dips on floor are one of the most effective exercises to increase arm strength and also build lean muscle in your upper arms.
Triceps dips on floor are a closed kinetic chain exercise and express that you do the movements around a fixed point. It increases compression force on your joints thereby improving stability.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','triceps','shoulders','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1320','CC-BY-SA 4','hektkaso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1324','Bodyweight lunge HD','Bodyweight lunge HD','Bodyweight lunges are an effective calisthenic exercise for
strengthening the lower body, improving balance and stability, and
developing functional strength. They are a popular choice for bodyweight workouts, home workouts, and can also be included as part of a larger strength training routine.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1324','CC-BY-SA 4','hektkaso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
