Execute slowly','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','hamstrings','calves']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1366','CC-BY-SA 4','Anastasious','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_137','Butterfly Narrow Grip','Butterfly Narrow Grip','The movement is the same as with a regular butterfly, only that the grip is narrow:

Sit on the butterfly machine, the feet have a good contact with the floor, the upper arms are parallel to the floor. Press your arms together till the handles are practically together (but aren''t!). Go slowly back. The weights should stay all the time in the air.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','137','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1370','Dumbbell Deadlift','Dumbbell Deadlift','Controlled execution
Don''t use momentum
Slow execution','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1370','CC-BY-SA 4','Anastasious','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1372','Triceps Dips (Assisted)','Triceps Dips (Assisted)','Assisted triceps dips  is a gym work out exercise that targets triceps and also involves chest.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1372','CC-BY-SA 4','matpn','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1373','box jumps','box jumps','Jump from a standing position onto the box, stretch your body, then step down again (do not jump)','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1373','CC-BY-SA 4','tekknokrat@gmx.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1374','Rotary Torso Machine','Rotary Torso Machine','Slow and Steady
Not too much weight','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1374','CC-BY-SA 4','6LXBO','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1376','Recumbent Bike','Recumbent Bike','For this exercise Recumbent Bike is needed. You just sit on it, set level and time and start the workout','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','calves','glutes','quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1376','CC-BY-SA 4','pera_perkan','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1377','Torso Twist','Torso Twist','Standing Torso Twist WorkoutTarget your core and improve flexibility with this dynamic standing exercise! The Standing Torso Twist Workout involves twisting your torso while keeping your feet and hips stable, engaging your obliques, and stretching your entire upper body. This movement helps to:Strengthen core musclesIncrease flexibility in the spine and torsoImprove posture and balanceEnhance overall athletic performancePerform 3 sets of 10-15 reps, twisting to each side, to feel the benefits of this effective and efficient workout!','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1377/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1377','CC-BY-SA 4','brucem','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1378','Cable Lateral Raises (Single Arm)','Cable Lateral Raises (Single Arm)','The single arm cable lateral raise is a variation of the lateral raise and an exercise used to build the muscles of the shoulders.

Position a cable at the lowest position possible and attach a single handle.
Reach across your body and grab the handle with a neutral grip.
Keep the elbow slightly bent and pull the handle across your body and raise laterally.
Slowly lower the handle back to the starting position under control.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1378/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1378','CC-BY-SA 4','carlos3c','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1380','Band pull-aparts','Band pull-aparts','Hold the band with your arms extended in front of you at shoulder height.
Keep your elbows slightly bent but fixed throughout the movement.
Pull the band apart by spreading your arms until the band touches or comes close to your chest.
Slowly bring your arms back to the starting position, controlling the tension on the band.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1380','CC-BY-SA 4','schwolfar','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1381','Upper Back','Upper Back','Upper Back is suitable for building up the core muscles with a special focus on the deltoid and rhomboid muscles and the upper back muscles','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1381','CC-BY-SA 4','phpi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1384','Pullover Machine','Pullover Machine','Pullover machine, sitting, elbows on pads','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','chest','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1384','CC-BY-SA 4','Paul@Chemistry','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1387','Hamstring Kicks','Hamstring Kicks','Stand with your feet hip-width apart and extend one arm in front of you. Swing that leg up in front of you and back down while keeping your leg as straight as possible and your toes pointed up.Repeat with the other leg.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1387/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1387','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1388','Single Leg RDL','Single Leg RDL','Stand upright and hold weights in both hands if using loads.
Brace your core and lift one leg off the ground.
Keep your back straight, hinge at the hips while lowering your torso forward, ensuring you don’t rotate your hips.
Lower until you feel a stretch in your standing leg''s hamstring, then return to standing position. Repeat on both sides.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1388','CC-BY-SA 4','admin','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_139','Butterfly Reverse','Butterfly Reverse',NULL,'SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','139','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1390','Toe Touch','Toe Touch','Stand with your feet closer together. Hinge at your hips and lower your upper body towards your toes. Reach your hands towards your feet, try to touch your toes, the ground, or as far down your legs as you can comfortably go.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1390','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1391','Elephant Walks','Elephant Walks','Hinge at your hips until you feel a stretch behind your knees. Bend one leg while the other is straight then fluidly bend the other knee while straightening the first knee.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1391','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1392','Good Morning','Good Morning','Stand with your feet more than shoulder-width apart (wider stance) and place your hands on your hips. Hinge at your hips and lower your upper body towards the ground while keeping your back straight then come back up.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1392/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1392','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1393','Single Leg Hamstring Stretch','Single Leg Hamstring Stretch','Sit on the ground with one leg straight out in front of you and the other leg bent in toward you. Reach forward with both hands, trying to touch the toes of your straight leg.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1393','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1394','Sit & Reach','Sit & Reach','Sit on the ground with your legs extended straight in front of you. Reach both hands forward, trying to reach past your toes or as far as you can go. Return to the starting position and repeat.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1394','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1395','Crossbody Leg Swings','Crossbody Leg Swings','Hold onto a wall or something near you for support. Swing one leg across the front of your body, then back and out to the side. Repeat while slowly increasing your range of motion.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1395','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1396','Standing Pancake','Standing Pancake','Stand and open your legs as wide as possible into a straddle position. Then bend at the hips, pushing them back while keeping your back straight.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1396','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1397','Standing Pancake Good Morning','Standing Pancake Good Morning','Stand with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart and toes pointed slightly outward. Place your hands on the back of your head. Hinge at your hips and lower your upper body towards the ground, keeping your back straight and chest open.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1397','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1398','Hamstring Chokes','Hamstring Chokes','Sit on the ground and bend one leg, bringing your knee toward you. Place your hand behind your hamstring and gently pull your leg toward your chest, feeling a stretch in the back of your thigh. Straighten your leg, extending up toward the ceiling.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1398','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1399','Roll Down','Roll Down','Stand with your feet hip-width apart and slowly roll your upper body forward, one vertebra at a time, until your hands touch the ground or as far as you can comfortably go. Roll back up to the starting position in the same controlled manner.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1399','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1400','Crossbody Hamstring Stretch','Crossbody Hamstring Stretch','While standing, cross one leg behind the other (keep this leg straight). Reach downward and try to touch the toes of that leg. Slightly bend the other leg so that you can bend down.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1400','CC-BY-SA 4','captive0592','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1406','Plank-to-Elbow Extension','Plank-to-Elbow Extension','The Plank-to-Elbow Extension is a dynamic exercise that combines the plank with an elbow extension movement','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CORE','ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','core','triceps','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1406','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1407','Cossack squat','Cossack squat','The Cossack Squat is a multi-joint exercise that works mainly on the legs and buttocks, but also involves stabilizing muscles. It is an excellent exercise for improving strength, mobility and stability in a functional way.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','calves','core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1407','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1408','Wall-sit','Wall-sit','The Wall Sit (or wall chair) is an isometric exercise that mainly involves the leg muscles, improving muscular endurance and stability. Here are the main and secondary muscles activated during the exercise.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','calves','core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1408','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1409','Dragon-flag','Dragon-flag','Keep your body completely rigid throughout the movement, avoiding sagging in your lower back.
Use a firm grip to stabilize your upper body.
Start with simpler versions (such as with bent knees) to build strength and control.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','SHOULDERS','LEGS','BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['core','shoulders','glutes','lats','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1409','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1410','Plank with Alternating Leg Lift','Plank with Alternating Leg Lift','In a plank position, lift one leg alternately.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs','alternating',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1410','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1411','Heel Touches','Heel Touches','Starting Position:

Lie on your back on an exercise mat.
Bend your knees, keeping your feet flat on the floor and hip-width apart.
Place your arms along your sides, palms facing inward, just off the floor.

Engage Core:

Lift your head, shoulders, and upper back slightly off the ground.
Keep your neck neutral and chin slightly tucked.

Perform the Movement:

Side-bend to the right, reaching your right hand toward your right heel.
Return to the center, then side-bend to the left, reaching your left hand toward your left heel.
Continue alternating sides in a controlled manner.

Breathing:

Exhale as you reach toward your heel and inhale as you return to the center.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1411','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1412','bicycle crunches','bicycle crunches','Bicycle crunches are a core exercise performed on the floor. Lie on your back with your hands behind your head and legs extended. Lift your shoulders off the ground, bring one knee toward your chest, and twist your torso so your opposite elbow meets the knee. Alternate sides in a pedaling motion, ensuring controlled movements and engaging your core throughout the exercise.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1412','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1414','Hack Squats','Hack Squats','Hack squats target the lower body and are performed on a hack squat machine or with a barbell. For the machine variation, position yourself on the platform with your shoulders under the pads and feet slightly forward. Push through your heels to lift the weight, then bend your knees to lower the platform in a controlled motion until your thighs are parallel to the ground. Push back up to the starting position. For the barbell variation, hold the bar behind your legs with your arms extended and perform a squat-like motion.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','hamstrings','calves','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1414','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1415','Dumbbell Crunches','Dumbbell Crunches','Dumbbell crunches are a weighted variation of traditional crunches designed to target the abdominal muscles more intensely. Lie flat on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor. Hold a dumbbell with both hands close to your chest or above your head. Lift your shoulders and upper back off the ground in a crunching motion, engaging your core. Slowly lower yourself back to the starting position. Ensure controlled movements throughout the exercise to prevent strain.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1415','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_142','Cable External Rotation','Cable External Rotation','Steps:

Start off placing an extension band around a post or in a secure position where it will not release and is at elbow level.
Position yourself to the side of the band and with your hand that is opposite of the band, reach out and grab the handle.
Bring the band to your chest keeping your elbow bent in a 90 degree angle then slowly rotate your arm in a backhand motion so that the band externally rotates out
Continue out as far as possible so that you feel a stretch in your shoulders, hold for a count and then return back to the starting position.
Repeat for as many reps and sets as desired.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','142','CC-BY-SA 3','lauroernesto','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1424','Biceps Curl Machine','Biceps Curl Machine','The biceps curl machine is designed to isolate the biceps muscles and provide a controlled range of motion. Sit on the machine with your back against the pad and adjust the seat so your arms are aligned with the machine''s handles or pads. Grip the handles firmly, keeping your elbows fixed in place, and curl the handles upward by contracting your biceps. Slowly lower the handles to the starting position, maintaining control throughout the movement.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1424','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1425','Toe Taps','Toe Taps','Toe taps are a core-focused exercise performed lying on your back. Lie flat with your arms by your sides and your legs raised to a tabletop position (knees bent at 90 degrees). Slowly lower one foot to gently tap the floor, keeping your core engaged and your lower back pressed into the ground. Return to the starting position and alternate legs. This exercise strengthens the core while minimizing strain on the lower back.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1425','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1426','Standing Side Crunches','Standing Side Crunches','Standing side crunches are a dynamic exercise that targets the obliques while improving balance and stability. Stand upright with your feet shoulder-width apart and hands behind your head or holding a dumbbell in one hand. Lean your torso to one side, contracting your obliques, while bringing your elbow toward your hip (or crunching toward the weight if using a dumbbell). Return to the starting position and alternate sides or perform all repetitions on one side before switching.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1426','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1429','Dumbbell Shoulder Rotations','Dumbbell Shoulder Rotations','Dumbbell shoulder rotations are designed to strengthen the rotator cuff muscles and improve shoulder stability and mobility.

External Rotation: Hold a dumbbell in one hand, keeping your elbow bent at 90 degrees and close to your body. Rotate your forearm outward, away from your body, keeping your elbow stationary. Slowly return to the starting position.
Internal Rotation: Hold a dumbbell in one hand, keeping your elbow bent at 90 degrees and close to your body. Rotate your forearm inward, toward your body, and slowly return to the starting position. Perform the exercise with controlled movements to avoid strain.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1429','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1430','Plate Pinch Hold','Plate Pinch Hold','The plate pinch hold is a grip strength exercise designed to target the forearms and improve grip endurance. Select one or two weight plates (smooth-edged plates work best) and pinch them together between your thumb and fingers. Hold the plates with your arm straight down by your side or extended slightly in front of you. Maintain the hold for as long as you can, keeping your shoulders relaxed and your grip firm. This exercise can be done for time or repetitions.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1430','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1433','Reverse Wood Chops','Reverse Wood Chops','Attach a looping resistance band to a rack below knee height
Grip the other end of the band like holding a baseball bat with both hands
Stretch the band facing it
Start with your hands at the side of your hips, knees bent
Rotate your hips while moving your hands towards over the top of your opposite shoulder
Imagine the motion as striking a baseball with a bat','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','BACK','SHOULDERS','ARMS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','lats','shoulders','biceps','quads','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1433','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1434','Lat Pull DB','Lat Pull DB','Bend upper body forward
Move dumbbells near your body with slightly bent arms towards your back','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1434','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1435','Scapula Pulls','Scapula Pulls','Hang straight on a pull-up bar
Pull shoulder blades together, moving the body slightly up','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1435','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1436','Pin Bench Press BB','Pin Bench Press BB','Set security pins to about the height of your sticking point
Lower the bar, rest on the pins for 1s while holding tension
Move bar up with maximum force','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1436','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1437','Pin Squat','Pin Squat','Set security pins to about the height of your sticking point
Lower the bar, rest on the pins for 2s keeping tension
Stand up with maximum force','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','quads','core']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1437','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1438','Clean','Clean','Regular olympic lift clean.
Pull bar from ground, catch on shoulders performing a front squat.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','hamstrings','lats','core']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1438','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1439','Pin OHP','Pin OHP','Set security pins to the height of your lower chin
Rest bar on pins keeping tension
Raise bar over head','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1439','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1440','Push OHP','Push OHP','Rest bar in front on your shoulders
Bend knees while keeping upper body straight
Extend legs pushing the bar overhead with force','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes','quads','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1440','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1441','Incline OHP DB','Incline OHP DB','Sit on a bench with 45° incline
Ellbows 45° out
Move dumbbells down until upper arms are parallel to shoulders
Move dumbbells up, meeting overhead','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1441','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1442','Kreis Press DB','Kreis Press DB','Sit on a bench with 45° incline
Hold dumbbells overhead
Move dumbbells down as if doing overhead press
Rotate dumbbells palms facing up and extend your arms in front of your body
Move hands together until dumbbells meet, keep arms extended
Reverse the motion until dumbbells are overhead again
This is one repetition','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','CHEST','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','chest','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1442','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1443','Shoulder Raise Side and Front DB','Shoulder Raise Side and Front DB','Stand while holding dumbbells beside body
Keep arms almost fully extended
Without momentum raise dumbbells to the side of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down
Lower dumbbells beside body, palms facing inwards
Immediately raise dumbbells in front of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down
Down again
This is one repetition','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1443','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1445','Jerk OL','Jerk OL','Olympic lift jerk

Hold bar in front on shoulders like push press
Bend and extend knees pushing bar up while diving under the bar
Catch bar overhead with straight arms using lunge
Move feet parallel while holding bar in lockout','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes','quads','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1445','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1446','Clean and Jerk OL','Clean and Jerk OL','Olympic lift clean and jerk.
Combination of clean and jerk in one motion.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','BACK','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','hamstrings','glutes','quads','lats','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1446','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1447','Snatch OL','Snatch OL','Olympic lift snatch

Pull barbell from ground to overhead lockout using a wide grip and overhead squat.
Move bar slowly until cleared knees then explosively extend hips, pull bar up and dive under the bar
Catch bar overhead with straight arms
Push head forward during lockout','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','hamstrings','glutes','quads','lats']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1447','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1448','Seated W Curl','Seated W Curl','Sit on bench with 60° incline
Hold dumbbells beside body near the ground, palms facing outwards, arms fully extended
Move dumbbells up using only biceps and without momentum','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1448/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1448','CC-BY-SA 4','M9','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1449','ClimbMill','ClimbMill','The ClimbMill, also known as a stair climber, is a cardio-focused machine that simulates climbing stairs. It provides an effective way to improve endurance while strengthening the lower body. To use the machine, step onto the moving stairs, maintain an upright posture, and use the handrails for balance if needed. Adjust the speed and intensity to match your fitness level. This exercise helps improve cardiovascular health, burns calories, and enhances lower body muscle endurance.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','hamstrings','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1449','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_145','Cable Woodchoppers','Cable Woodchoppers','Set cable pulley slightly lower than chest height. Keep body facing forward with hips stable.  Grab the pulley handle, fully extend your arms and bring your arms forward and across your body. Hold for 1 second at the end of the movement and slowly return to starting position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','145','CC-BY-SA 3','robhoyt','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1450','Cobra Stretch','Cobra Stretch','The Cobra Stretch is a back extension exercise that helps improve spinal flexibility and relieve lower back tension. To perform, lie face down on the floor with your hands placed under your shoulders. Press your palms into the floor and lift your chest while keeping your hips on the ground. Keep your elbows slightly bent and your shoulders relaxed. Hold the stretch for a few seconds, then slowly lower yourself back down. This exercise is beneficial for improving posture and reducing lower back stiffness.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['core','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1450','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1451','Torso rotation stretch','Torso rotation stretch','The torso rotation stretch helps improve spinal mobility and relieves tension in the lower back and obliques. It can be performed standing or seated.

Standing Variation: Stand upright with your feet shoulder-width apart. Place your hands on your hips or extend your arms in front of you. Slowly rotate your torso to one side, keeping your hips stable. Hold for a few seconds, then rotate to the opposite side.
Seated Variation: Sit on a chair with your feet flat on the floor. Place one hand on the outside of your opposite thigh and gently twist your torso toward that side. Hold the stretch before switching sides.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1451','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1452','Knee to Chest Stretch','Knee to Chest Stretch','The knee to chest stretch is a simple yet effective exercise for relieving lower back tension and improving hip mobility. To perform, lie flat on your back with your legs extended. Bring one knee toward your chest, wrapping your hands around your shin or behind your thigh. Gently pull the knee closer to your chest while keeping the other leg straight on the floor. Hold the stretch for 15–30 seconds, then switch sides. For a deeper stretch, both knees can be pulled toward the chest simultaneously.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1452/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1452','CC-BY-SA 4','hpmbala@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1455','Towel Superman','Towel Superman','In this exercise, you lie flat on your stomach, hold a
towel with your arms extended in front of you, and pull it apart to
create tension. Then, you move it forward and back under your stomach.
This exercise targets the back and shoulder muscles as well as core
stability.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1455','CC-BY-SA 4','Yderkone','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1457','Cable Press Around','Cable Press Around','Set the cable pulley at chest height and attach a D-handle bar. Grab
the handle with a neutral grip and hold it next to your chest with your
elbow fully flexed and tight to your side. Turn away from the pulley so
your torso is at 45 degrees.

Hold the other side of the functional trainer with your corresponding hand. Assume a staggered stance for better balance.

While keeping your chest proud, extend your elbow at 45 degrees
across your midline while keeping your arm parallel to the floor. Stop
shy of lockout and contract your chest at the top of the range of motion
(ROM).','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest','triceps','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1457','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1458','Cross-Body Cable Y-Raise','Cross-Body Cable Y-Raise','Attach a D-Bar to the cable machine. Perform a motion akin to drawing a sword from across your body.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1458','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_146','Calf Press Using Leg Press Machine','Calf Press Using Leg Press Machine','Put  the balls of your feet on an extended leg press pad.  Use your calves to press the weight by flexing your feet/toes into a pointed position, and releasing back into a relaxed position.

This exercise builds mass and strength in the Gastrocnemius and Soleus muscles as well, if not better, than any calf exercise.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Calves',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_146/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','146','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1461','No Leg Drive Dumbbell Chest Press','No Leg Drive Dumbbell Chest Press','Set up for a normal Dumbbell chest press but lift your leg ups straight or put them on another bench to remove the leg drive.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1461','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1462','punches','punches','stand stable and throw normal straight punches','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1462','CC-BY-SA 4','lh1701','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1463','Dumbbell Underhand Dead Row','Dumbbell Underhand Dead Row','The Dumbbell Underhand Dead Row will involve the back, which means you can try a bit heavier weight. The catch is that you need to be able to control the weight for all the reps.

Start by holding a pair of dumbbells with your feet shoulder-wide apart and your knees slightly bent.
Hinge at your hips to lower your torse forward until it''s almost parallel to the floor, keeping your back flat and maintaining a slight bend in your knees.
Exhale as you row the dumbbells to your sides up to chest height, leading with your elbows until your upper arms are just past parallel to the floor and the dumbbells are at ribcage level.
Slowly lower to the starting position and repeat. Keep your back flat all the time.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1463','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1464','Pause Hack Squats','Pause Hack Squats','Hack Squats but with a 1-2s pause at the bottom of the movement. This makes sure that there is no more elastic energy stored in the muscles.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','hamstrings','calves','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1464','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1465','Spider Curl','Spider Curl','To get the most out of DB Spider Curls, you need an
adjustable weight bench set at a 45-degree incline. This inclined position
allows your arms to hang freely, putting them in an extended start position
with elbows slightly in front of your torso, which is the key to maintaining
low-level isometric tension throughout the movement pattern.

Lie face-down on an adjustable
weight bench with your chest fully supported, holding a pair of dumbbells.
Keep a neutral head position
and don’t crane your neck.
Let your arms hang straight
down with your palms facing forward (for a standard Spider Curl) or palms
facing inward for a Hammer Curl exercise variation.
Keep a stable foot position on
the floor to maintain balance and control.
Start the curl motion by
flexing your biceps muscles and lifting the pair of dumbbells or curl bar
toward your shoulders.
Keep your elbow flexion
controlled. Your arms should stay locked in position with no unnecessary
movement.
Squeeze hard at the top for 1-2 seconds. This
is where maximum tension hits the biceps muscle fibers.
Lower the weight under control
for 3-4 seconds to keep muscles under tension for the entire range of
motion.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1465','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1466','Calf Raise using Hack Squat Machine','Calf Raise using Hack Squat Machine','Ideally using a trapeze addon, Lift the weight up using your calves by getting on your toes.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1466','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1467','Incline Close Grip Barbell Bench Press','Incline Close Grip Barbell Bench Press','Narrower grip than regular bench press, just outside shoulder width.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','shoulders','chest']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1467','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1468','Floor Skull Crusher','Floor Skull Crusher','Allowing you to safely load more weight than a regular skull crusher, lie on the floor and rest the weight on the floor in between each repetition.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1468','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1469','Bent over Cable Flye','Bent over Cable Flye','Holding your upper body at an approximate 105° angle.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1469','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1470','1-Arm Half-Kneeling Lat Pulldown','1-Arm Half-Kneeling Lat Pulldown','Attach a D-Handle to a high pully. And use your lat muscles to pull the weight single handedly.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1470','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1471','Kroc Row','Kroc Row','Dumbbell rows with looser technique but heavier weight.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1471','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1472','Cable Shrug-In','Cable Shrug-In','Attach two D-Handles to two low cables and shrug in using your upper traps.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1472','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1473','Reverse Cable Flye','Reverse Cable Flye','Attach D-Handles to two cable pulleys in the upper position. Grab the left on with your right hand and vice-versa.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1473','CC-BY-SA 4','Expenses7000','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1474','W-Raise','W-Raise','This challenging exercise is a variation of reverse crunches that is made up of three parts in which we’re basically drawing an upside down ‘W’ with our legs.
Start position is lying face up flat on the floor with legs extended at the low point of the outer leg of the ‘W’. Keeping a strong core and legs straight, go up, rise your hips and then slowly lower your legs down halfway. Then, lifting your legs back up to the top, rise your hips again, maintaining that straight line, use your core strength to finally come back all the way down to the other outer leg of the W. Then you reverse the ‘W’ to return to the start.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1474','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1475','Black Widow Knee Slides','Black Widow Knee Slides','In
this bottom-up rotation exercise movement, you’ll cross your knee over and
drive it into that opposite elbow. Start in high plank position (or tabletop
position) with hands directly beneath your shoulders. Lift the left knee toward
the right arm and slide it up the forearm to get more of that posterior pelvic
tilt and engagement of the abdominal muscles. Then do the opposite side,
bringing your right knee toward your left hand.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1475','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1476','Butterfly Sit Up','Butterfly Sit Up','In
this midrange exercise your arm muscles provide you with a little bit of
momentum to help to get you off the ground. You also open them up in overhead
position which engages the upper back. Start
lying with feet flat on the ground, knees at an angle, arms crossed in towards your chest. Using
your ab muscles, bring your upper body off the ground as you open your arms
into goal post position, then slowly lower yourself back down to return to
starting position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1476','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1477','Seated Corkscrew','Seated Corkscrew','To
do this abs and obliques exercise, start with your hands back behind your body
and bring your knees in and across, really trying to contract the obliques.
Then extend your legs back out to starting position and repeat toward the
opposite side of the abs.
Beginners
might find that they can’t even get through the first 45 seconds of this
challenging reverse crunches variation.  That’s ok because it gives you a
place to start and something to improve upon.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1477','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1478','Levitation Crunch','Levitation Crunch','For
this top down movement, we’re trying to move the upper torso without moving the
lower torso. Start lying on the ground with feet flat on the floor and crossed
arms above your head with hands behind head. Lift upper body up and clear your
shoulder blades off the ground and then hold and pause at the top for a one or
two count. Try to make the upper abs work and hold that contraction for 10 good
quality reps.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1478','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1479','Sit Up Elbow Thrust','Sit Up Elbow Thrust','This
is a top down rotation movement, and it’s a bit more
explosive, too.
Lying with knees bent and feet on the floor, sit up and then drive your left elbow across your entire body toward the right, then come back
to center and then finally lower yourself down. Then hit the other side.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1479/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1479','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_148','Calf Raises on Hackenschmitt Machine','Calf Raises on Hackenschmitt Machine','Place yourself on the machine with your back firmly against the backrest, the feet are on the platform for calf raises. Check that the feet are half free and that you can completely stretch the calf muscles down.

With straight knees pull up your weight as much as you can. Go with a fluid movement down till the calves are completely stretched. Repeat.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Calves',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','148','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1480','Lying Triceps Extensions','Lying Triceps Extensions','Starting position for this
practical triceps exercise is lying on a standard bench holding a barbell or two dumbbells in both hands with an overhand grip, hands at shoulder width apart.
Begin with arms over your upper
chest and elbows bent back at about a 45-degree angle.
First bend at the elbows and
then allow the upper arm to drop back, bringing the barbell/dumbbells behind your
head and down toward the floor. In terms of upper arm position, the barbell/dumbbells should never be fully above your head, but instead behind it, to
ensure that you’re targeting the triceps.
Keep the shoulder blades tucked
under, the elbows tight in toward your head and your core active during
this entire movement.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1480','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1481','Drag Pushdown','Drag Pushdown','Starting
position for this rope pushdown is standing facing a cable machine with
the handles of a rope attachment in both hands and feet shoulder width
apart.
Hinge
forward slightly at the hips maintaining an upright chest and bring the
shoulders and elbows behind the body so that when you push down on the
cable attachments, you can get a fully contracted triceps long head.
Drag
the cable machine rope attachment as close to the body as possible and
straighten your elbows until lockout.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1481','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1482','Dumbbell Cheat Curl','Dumbbell Cheat Curl','Starting position is standing
with feet shoulder width apart.
Hands should take an underhand
or supinated grip on the dumbbells holding them with hands shoulder
width apart.
Keeping elbows tucked into your
sides throughout the entire movement, use momentum to curl the dumbbells,
squeezing your biceps at the top of the movement.
Slowly lower to return to the
starting position. Keep the core tight throughout the exercise.

Cheating
through the concentric curling portion of this challenging exercise gives us a
great opportunity to increase time under tension and create eccentric overload
with heavier weight when we lower.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1482','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1483','Bizeps Curls Trifecta','Bizeps Curls Trifecta','This exercise is a mixture of three different curls: the Supinated Cross Body Curl, the Pronated Cross Body Curl and the No Money Curl. You
alternate between three curl variations that each accomplish different goals,
and you’ll keep the set going beyond the usual 8-12 rep range which gives
us that intensity.

For the Supinated Cross Body
Curl, supinate the forearm with palms facing toward the ceiling and
forearms coming across the body. Lift the inner-facing weight of the dumbbell towards your shoulder.
For the Pronated Cross Body
Curl, pronate the forearm with palms facing toward the floor (pronated
grip or overhand grip) and forearms coming across the body. Lift the inner-facing weight of the dumbbell towards your shoulder.
For the No Money Curl, you’ll
curl the dumbbell as you outwardly rotate the shoulder. Lift the inner-facing weight of the dumbbell towards your outer side of the shoulder.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1483','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1484','Omni Cable Cross-over','Omni Cable Cross-over','Adjust the weights based on the
motion. When pulling from top to bottom, increase the weight by 20% to 40%
more than the bottom-to-top motion. This accounts for the fact that when
operating from top down, the upper chest muscles are naturally weaker than
the lower chest muscles. So, adjust your weight stack to
compensate.

Position one cable at a high
setting and the other at the lowest level setting. Get into a staggered
stance in between the cable towers.
For the cable set low, pull it
upward and across your body. This effectively targets the upper chest.
For the cable set high, draw it
downward and across your body. This will primarily engage the lower chest.

Once you’re done, swap the
positions of the cables. Change the previously high cable to the lowest
position and vice versa. Repeat the exercise sequence, ensuring you’re
targeting both chest regions effectively.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1484','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1485','Rocking Triceps Pushdown','Rocking Triceps Pushdown','Set your feet below the rope and lean your upper body towards the rope. Set one foot back. Push down the rope and lean your entire body back onto the rear foot as you push down to get your hands behind your body. Don''t forget to bring your chest to the front during the pushdown. As you release the rope slowly, lean your body back onto the front foot.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1485','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1486','Alternating High Cable Row','Alternating High Cable Row','Start
by putting the attachment in a high position on the cable station and step back about 1m from the attachment. Grab
the cable pulley handle in your left hand at about head height with your elbow slightly bent. Step back with your left foot.
Pull
your elbow joint in toward the torso twisting slightly and perform a
single-arm row. Engage the lats as you twist.
Return
to the starting position with cable pulley and left foot and grab the cable pulley handle in the right
hand. Repeat this motion on the opposite side with your right foot stepped back.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back','alternating',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1486','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1487','Hyper Y W Combo','Hyper Y W Combo','Use a glute-ham raise or a
stability ball for this exercise and a light weight plate in each hand.
Raise your torso to form a straight line with your legs and raise the
arms outward slightly beyond a 90-degree angle into a W position to hit
the rotator cuff muscles, and then lower back to the starting position.
Then raise up again with arms
in a Y position to activate the lower traps.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1487','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1489','Plank Jacks','Plank Jacks','Jumping jacks from the plank position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','core','calves','quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1489','CC-BY-SA 4','jayninja','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1490','Lying Triceps Kickback','Lying Triceps Kickback','Set the bench to an 60deg angle. Stand still and rest your upper body on the inclined bench, ensuring a nearly straight line of your entire body. Squeeze your shoulder blades together, so that your elbows are located behind your torso with your upper arms nearly parallel to the floor. Lift the dumbbells until your arms form a straight line. Slowly lower the dumbbells back to the initial position. Initial position corresponds to an rectangular position of upper and lower arms.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1490','CC-BY-SA 4','Moffi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1492','High Row','High Row','Kneeling down on one leg and pulling cable down while driving elbow into the lats.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1492','CC-BY-SA 4','aahuja','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1493','Bayesian Curl','Bayesian Curl','Cable curl with stretched shoulder (backwards)','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1493','CC-BY-SA 4','aahuja','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1496','DB Upper Chest Variation','DB Upper Chest Variation','Dumbbell in hand in a curl fashion, lean body into the arm to help the dumbbell up above the chest, next to the head, to activate chest and delt combo','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1496','CC-BY-SA 4','JohnPreston','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
