Position: Rest the bar on your upper chest.
Press: Brace your core and push the bar straight up until your arms lock out.
Finish: Control the bar back down to your chest.
https://youtu.be/ZXpdJOLNoWw?si=u27cGyODoblXHBu1','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1893/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1893','CC-BY-SA 4','nishant0712','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1900','Tricep Rope Pushdowns','Tricep Rope Pushdowns','Setup: Stand facing the cable, feet shoulder-width apart, with a slight forward lean.
Grip: Hold the rope with palms facing each other and elbows tucked tight to your ribs.
Execution: Push the rope down until arms are fully straight, pulling the ends apart at the bottom.
Control: Keep upper arms still and return to the start with a slow, controlled motion.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1900/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1900','CC-BY-SA 4','nishant0712','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1901','Clean and Press','Clean and Press','The First Pull: Lift the bar from the floor to knee-height by driving with the legs, keeping the angle of your back constant.
The "Power" Position: As the bar reaches mid-thigh, explosively shrug and extend your hips to create vertical momentum.
The Quick Elbow Turnover: In the catch phase, rotate your elbows rapidly under the bar to create a "shelf" on your front deltoids.
The Vertical Press: Press the bar in a straight line; your head should shift slightly forward once the bar clears your forehead to reach full lockout.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','quads']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1901/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1901','CC-BY-SA 4','nishant0712','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1902','Weighted push-ups','Weighted push-ups','Setup: Begin in a standard plank position with a weight plate balanced securely on your upper back.
Alignment: Maintain a straight line from your head to your heels, engaging your core to prevent your back from sagging.
Execution: Lower your body until your chest nearly touches the floor, keeping your elbows at a forty-five degrees.
Ascent: Press through your palms to return to the starting position, fully extending your arms.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1902/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1902','CC-BY-SA 4','nishant0712','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
