('wger_1962','Step Jack','Step Jack','The Step Jack is a low-impact plyometric-style move that provides cardiovascular benefits without the joint stress of jumping. It works the entire body, specifically targeting the legs, core, and shoulders. This move is ideal for beginners, individuals with joint sensitivities, or as a dynamic warm-up to gradually elevate the heart rate.
Notes (Instructions):

​Stand upright with your feet together and arms at your sides.
​Step your right foot out to the side while simultaneously swinging both arms up above your head.
Bring your right foot back to the center and lower your arms.
​Immediately repeat the movement, stepping out with your left foot.
​Continue alternating sides at a steady, rhythmic pace.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','SHOULDERS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['quads','shoulders','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1962/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1962','CC-BY-SA 4','Anon#2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1963','Slow Squat','Slow Squat','​A tempo-based squat that uses controlled movement to increase muscle tension and improve lower-body stability.

​Lower: Descend slowly for 3 seconds.
​Pause: Hold at the bottom for 1 second.
​Stand: Return to the starting position at a normal pace.
Form: Keep your chest up and weight in your heels.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['quads','hamstrings','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1963/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1963','CC-BY-SA 4','Anon#2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1964','Wide Push-Up','Wide Push-Up','​A push-up variation with a wider hand placement to increase the emphasis on the outer chest muscles and shoulders.

​Setup: Place hands wider than shoulder-width apart on the floor.
Lower: Descend until your chest nearly touches the floor, keeping your core tight.
​Push: Drive through your palms to return to the start position.
​Form: Don''t let your lower back sag; keep a straight line from head to heels.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1964','CC-BY-SA 4','Anon#2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1965','Marching High Knees','Marching High Knees','A low-impact cardio and mobility exercise that strengthens the hip flexors and improves balance.

​Movement: Stand tall and lift one knee toward your chest as high as comfortable.
​Arms: Swing the opposite arm forward as you lift your knee, similar to a walking motion.
​Core: Keep your abs engaged to maintain an upright posture.
​Pace: Perform the movement with control, alternating legs rhythmically.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['quads','calves','glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1965/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1965','CC-BY-SA 4','Anon#2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1966','1/2 Kneeling Thoracic Rotation','1/2 Kneeling Thoracic Rotation','Begin in a half kneeling position with the
leg away from the wall stabilized against the wall
with a ball.
With both hands directly in front of
you, rotate one arm open attempting to reach
the wall behind you.
Exhale as you rotate, inhale
as you return to neutral and repeat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1966','CC-BY-SA 4','amwang4','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1967','lento avanti seduto','lento avanti seduto','slow controlled seated forward exercise with dumbbells','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1967','CC-BY-SA 4','Cf','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1968','Single-arm dumbbell shoulder press','Single-arm dumbbell shoulder press','Press the dumbbell vertically overhead in a controlled motion until your arm is fully extended, without locking the elbow. Slowly lower the dumbbell back to the starting position at shoulder height.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1968/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1968','CC-BY-SA 4','evtimovgeorg','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1969','Single-arm cable pushdown','Single-arm cable pushdown','Single-arm cable pushdown is a unilateral isolation exercise that targets the triceps brachii. By working one arm at a time, it helps correct strength imbalances between sides while also engaging the core for stability.
Starting position:
Stand facing the cable machine with your feet shoulder-width apart. Attach a single handle to the high pulley. Grab the handle with one hand using an overhand grip (pronated), with your elbow bent at approximately 90° and tucked close to your body. Keep your core braced and your back straight.
Execution:
Push the handle downward in a controlled motion by extending your elbow until your arm is fully extended. Hold the contraction for 1 second at the bottom, then slowly return to the starting position.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1969','CC-BY-SA 4','evtimovgeorg','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_197','Dips Between Two Benches','Dips Between Two Benches','Put two benches so far appart, that you can hold onto one with your hands and are just able to reach the other with your feet. The legs stay during the exercise completely stretched. With your elbows facing back, bend them as much as you can. Push yourself up, but don''t stretch out the arms.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_197/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','197','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1970','Kettlebell sumo high pull','Kettlebell sumo high pull','A compound exercise combining elements of a sumo deadlift and a high pull. It targets the posterior chain, particularly the glutes, hamstrings, and upper back. The sumo stance increases hip engagement, while the high pull adds an explosive element, promoting power development.

Stand upright overtop of a kettlebell with your feet wider than shoulder-width apart angled out slightly.
Maintain a braced core and neutral spine throughout the exercise.
Hinge your hips backward and extend your arms to grab ahold the kettlebell with a double overhand grip.
With you lower legs nearly vertical to the ground, extend your hips to raise the kettlebell with your elbows high keeping it close to your body.
Once the kettlebell has reached shoulder height, lower back to the starting position.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','hamstrings','glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1970','CC-BY-SA 4','wgerpott','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1971','Mentzer Pulldown','Mentzer Pulldown','Close grip front facing Pull down, while focusing on Biceps, Increases activation of biceps over the whole range, Avoid activating Lats.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_1971/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1971','CC-BY-SA 4','Mike Mentzer','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_1972','Single-Arm Lat Pulldown','Single-Arm Lat Pulldown','Sit at the lat pulldown machine and grab the single handle with a neutral grip. Keep your torso stable, your chest lifted, and your shoulder blades slightly retracted. Start with your arm fully extended overhead, then pull the handle down toward your upper chest following a controlled, slightly diagonal path. Focus on engaging the latissimus dorsi while keeping the shoulder depressed and avoiding any torso rotation. Slowly return to the starting position, maintaining full control throughout the movement.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','1972','CC-BY-SA 4','evtimovgeorg','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_20','Arnold Shoulder Press','Arnold Shoulder Press','Very common shoulder exercise.

As shown here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vj2w851ZHRM','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','20','CC-BY-SA 3','trzr23','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_202','Dumbbell Concentration Curl','Dumbbell Concentration Curl','Sit on bench. Grasp dumbbell between feet. Place back of upper arm to inner thigh. Lean into leg to raise elbow slightly.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','202','CC-BY-SA 3','http://www.exrx.net/WeightExercises/Brachialis/DBC','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_203','Dumbbell Goblet Squat','Dumbbell Goblet Squat','Grasp dumbbell with both hands at the sides of the upper plates. Hold dumbbell in front of chest, close to torso. Place feet about shoulderwide apart, keep knees slightly bent.

Squat down until thighs are parallel to floor. Keep back straight, bend and move hips backward to keep knees above feet. Return, keep knees slightly flexed. Repeat.

Keep bodyweight on heels and look ahead or slightly above to keep back straight.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_203/0.jpeg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','203','CC-BY-SA 4','ataraxie67','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_204','Dumbbell Incline Curl','Dumbbell Incline Curl','Setup: Set an adjustable bench to an incline of approximately 45 to 60 degrees.
Starting Position: Sit back against the bench with a dumbbell in each hand. Let your arms hang straight down toward the floor with your palms facing forward (supinated grip).
The Curl: Keeping your upper arms stationary and shoulders pinned back against the bench, exhale and curl the weights upward toward your shoulders.
Peak Contraction: Squeeze your biceps hard at the top of the movement, ensuring your elbows do not swing forward.
The Descent: Inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells back to the starting position, maintaining full control and feeling the stretch in the biceps.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','204','CC-BY-SA 4','ExRx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_205','Dumbbell Lunges Standing','Dumbbell Lunges Standing','.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','205','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_206','Dumbbell Lunges Walking','Dumbbell Lunges Walking','Starting Position: Stand with feet hip-width apart and hands either on your hips or holding dumbbells at your sides.
The Stride: Take a wide step forward with your right leg.
The Descent: Lower your hips until both knees are bent at approximately 90-degree angles.
The Transition: Drive through your front heel to stand up, bringing your back foot forward to step directly into the next lunge.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_206/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','206','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_208','Dumbbells on Scott Machine','Dumbbells on Scott Machine',NULL,'ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','208','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_211','Dumbbell Triceps Extension','Dumbbell Triceps Extension','Position one dumbbell over head with both hands under inner plate (heart shaped grip).

With elbows over head, lower forearm behind upper arm by flexing elbows. Flex wrists at bottom to avoid hitting dumbbell on back of neck. Raise dumbbell over head by extending elbows while hyperextending wrists. Return and repeat.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','shoulders','chest']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','211','CC-BY-SA 3','tuninx','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_222','Facepull','Facepull','Attach a rope to a pulley station set at about chest level.

Step back so you''re supporting the weight with arms completely outstretched and assume a staggered (one foot forward) stance. Bend the knees slightly for a stable base.

Retract the scapulae (squeeze your partner''s finger with your shoulder blades) and pull the center of the rope slightly up towards the face. A good cue is to think about pulling the ends of the rope apart, not just pulling back.

As you near your face, externally rotate so your knuckles are facing the ceiling.

Hold for one second at the top position and slowly lower.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','222','CC-BY-SA 4','abeworld','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_235','Flutter Kicks','Flutter Kicks','-Laying on the back, lift your straightened legs from the ground at a 45 degree angle.

-As your Left foot travels downward and nearly touches the floor, your Right foot should seek to reach a 90 degree angle, or as close to one as possible.

-Bring your R foot down until it nearly touches the floor, and bring your L foot upwards.  Maintain leg rigidity throughout the exercise.  Your head should stay off the ground, supported by tightened upper abdominals.

-(L up R down, L down R up, x2)  ^v, v^, ^v, v^ = 1 rep

-Primarily works the Rectus Abdominus, the hip flexors and the lower back. Secondarily works the Obliques.  Emphasis placed on the lower quadrant of the abs.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','235','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_237','Fly With Cable','Fly With Cable','cable machine, two steps forward, straight back','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_237/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','237','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_238','Fly With Dumbbells','Fly With Dumbbells','Take two dumbbells and lay on a bench, make sure the feet are firmly on the ground and your back is not arched, but has good contact with the bench. The arms are stretched in front of you, about shoulder wide. Bend now the arms a bit and let them down with a half-circle movement to the side. Without changing the angle of the elbow bring them in a fluid movement back up.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_238/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','238','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_239','Fly With Dumbbells, Decline Bench','Fly With Dumbbells, Decline Bench','The exercise is the same as with a regular bench:

Take two dumbbells and lay on a bench, make sure the feet are firmly on the ground and your back is not arched, but has good contact with the bench. The arms are stretched in front of you, about shoulder wide. Bend now the arms a bit and let them down with a half-circle movement to the side. Without changing the angle of the elbow bring them in a fluid movement back up.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','239','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2447','Hip Airplane','Hip Airplane','Stand on one leg and lean your upper body slightly forward while keeping your back straight. Extend the free leg behind you so that your torso and leg form roughly one line. Slowly open your hip to the side by rotating your pelvis and upper body in a controlled way. Then close the hip again and return to the starting position.

The movement should mainly come from the hip. Keep your standing foot stable and avoid letting your knee collapse inward.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings','calves']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2447','CC-BY-SA 4','TobiasFalk','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2448','Reverse Clamshell','Reverse Clamshell','Lie on your side with your hips and knees bent, keeping your knees stacked on top of each other. Keep your feet together at first, then keep your knees touching while lifting your top foot upward. Slowly lower the foot back down with control.

Move only through the hip and avoid rolling your pelvis backward. The movement should be small, controlled, and focused on hip rotation.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2448','CC-BY-SA 4','TobiasFalk','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2449','Clamshell to Reverse Clamshell','Clamshell to Reverse Clamshell','Lie on your side with your hips and knees bent, keeping your legs stacked. Lift your top knee into a clamshell position and keep the leg elevated throughout the movement. From there, alternate between opening the knee upward and lifting the foot upward, moving through hip external and internal rotation.

Keep the movement slow and controlled. Do not let the top leg rest on the bottom leg between repetitions.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2449','CC-BY-SA 4','TobiasFalk','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_245','Skullcrusher Dumbbells','Skullcrusher Dumbbells','Hold the dumbbells and lay down on a flat bench in such a way that around 1/4 of your head is over the edge. Stretch arms straight up and then lean dumbbells away from your toes to a 10-20 degree angle. Keep upper arm at this angle throughout exercise. Dumbbell shall not be amed at your head, but away over your head. This will maximise gain from exercise with load on triceps all the time.

Pay attention to your elbows and arms: only the triceps are doing the work, the rest of the arms should not move.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','245','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2452','Curl De Muñeca Con Barra','Curl De Muñeca Con Barra','This is a variation of the flat bench press designed to emphasize the clavicular head of the pectoralis major (the upper portion). By tilting the torso, the angle of the push changes, shifting more tension to the upper chest and shoulders, which helps achieve a more aesthetic, balanced, and three-dimensional development of the torso.

Starting Position: Grip a bar with an overhand grip (palms facing up) at a width similar to your shoulders.

Position on the Bench: Kneel in front of a flat bench and rest the backs of your forearms on it. Your wrists and hands should extend slightly beyond the edge of the bench to allow for a full range of motion.

Eccentric Phase (Lowering): Lower the bar in a controlled manner by extending your wrists toward the floor. At the bottom of the movement, slightly spread your fingers to let the bar roll down a bit, maximizing the stretch.

Concentric Phase (Lift): First, close your fingers to secure the bar, then flex your wrists upward explosively but in a controlled manner, bringing the bar as high as possible. Strongly contract your forearms at the top position for one second.

Form: Keep your forearms firmly pressed against the bench throughout the exercise; only your wrists and fingers should move.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_2452/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2452','CC-BY-SA 4','xWan','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2454','YTW Raises','YTW Raises','The YTW exercise for scapular retraction is designed to strengthen the inter-scapular muscles between your shoulder blades, to help retract or pull your shoulders back, helping to maintain proper upright posture.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2454','CC-BY-SA 4','probablyforging','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_246','Skullcrusher SZ-bar','Skullcrusher SZ-bar','Hold the SZ-bar and lay down on a flat bench in such a way that around 1/4 of your head is over the edge. Stretch your arms with the bar and bend them so that the bar is lowered. Just before it touches your forehead, push it up.

Pay attention to your elbows and arms: only the triceps are doing the work, the rest of the arms should not move.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_246/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','246','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2478','Glute-Ham Raise','Glute-Ham Raise','Kneel on a glute-ham developer or have a partner hold your ankles. Keeping hips straight, lower your torso toward the floor under control, then curl back up by contracting the hamstrings and glutes.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2478','CC0','personal use','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2480','Easy Continuous Swim (Freestyle)','Easy Continuous Swim (Freestyle)','Swim freestyle at a relaxed, steady pace without stopping — think conversation pace, not racing. Focus on smooth, even strokes rather than speed or breathing technique; this is just to get your body moving and your heart rate up.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK','CHEST','LEGS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats','chest','hamstrings','calves','glutes','quads','core','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2480','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2481','Kick with Board','Kick with Board','Hold a kickboard with both hands, arms extended in front of you, face in the water (lift head forward to breathe when needed). Kick from your hips, not your knees, keeping your legs mostly straight with a slight bend and a steady, compact flutter kick. This builds leg endurance and keeps your body horizontal without needing to worry about your arms.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','hamstrings','calves','core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2481','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2482','Bobbing Exhale Drill','Bobbing Exhale Drill','Stand in chest-deep water. Take a breath, submerge your face fully, and exhale slowly and completely through your nose and/or mouth the whole time you''re underwater — a gentle humming sound can help keep the exhale steady and controlled. Once you''re empty of air, lift your head, take a fresh breath, and go back under. Repeat continuously. The goal is training your body that all your exhaling happens underwater, so all you need to do at the surface is inhale.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2482','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2483','Wall-Hold Rotation','Wall-Hold Rotation','Hold the pool wall or edge with one hand, body horizontal at the surface, legs kicking gently behind you. Keep your face in the water, exhaling continuously, then rotate your head to the side — not lifting it up — so one goggle stays in the water while the other clears the surface. Take a quick breath, then rotate your face back down to neutral. This isolates the head-rotation motion without any arm strokes to think about.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2483','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2484','Side-Kick Breathing (Kickboard)','Side-Kick Breathing (Kickboard)','Push off the wall on your side (not flat on your stomach), one arm extended forward holding the board or just extended, kicking continuously. Keep your head in a neutral position looking at the bottom of the pool, and when you need air, rotate your head sideways (one ear stays in the water, other faces up) to breathe, then rotate back to neutral. Swim a length like this, then repeat on the other side. This teaches the exact head position and rotation you''ll use once full stroke breathing comes in.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','shoulders','hamstrings','quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2484','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2485','Stroke-and-Roll Drill','Stroke-and-Roll Drill','Push off, swim a few strokes, and every breath roll fully onto your back for 2-3 breaths, then roll back into freestyle. This teaches you to rotate your body as a unit rather than just turning your head, and helps remove the fear of not having your face in the water.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats','core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2485','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2486','Recovery Bobbing','Recovery Bobbing','Same motion as the Bobbing Exhale Drill, but done in slightly deeper water (so you''re not touching the bottom) and at a slower, more relaxed pace — think of it as a recovery/reset exercise rather than a hard drill. Use it between harder drills to reset your breathing rhythm and calm down if you''re feeling rushed or out of sync.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2486','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2487','Cool-Down Swim','Cool-Down Swim','Swim at an easy, unhurried pace — freestyle, backstroke, or just floating/gliding — with zero focus on technique or drills. The only goal here is to let your heart rate come down gradually and your muscles relax before you get out of the pool.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK','CHEST','LEGS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats','chest','glutes','core','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2487','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2488','Posterior Pelvic Tilt','Posterior Pelvic Tilt','Lie on your back with knees bent, feet flat on the floor. Flatten your lower back against the floor by tilting your pelvis posteriorly, engaging your abs and glutes. Hold 5 seconds, release. This retrains pelvic positioning to counter anterior pelvic tilt.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['core','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2488','CC-BY-SA 4','Raj','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2489','Low row','Low row','Based on Low Row Sel. by Technogym. In this version, you use it with two arms.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2489','CC-BY-SA 4','lbroggi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2490','Pulley (low, with triangle)','Pulley (low, with triangle)','This exercise is based on Technogym Pulley Sel. Hold the triangle with both hands and bring the weight towards your belly.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2490','CC-BY-SA 4','lbroggi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2491','Abductors','Abductors','Based on Abductors Sel. by Technogym.
Position yourself on the machine and open your legs as much as possible.
Return slowly to the original position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2491','CC-BY-SA 4','lbroggi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2492','Adductors','Adductors','Based on Adductor Sel. by Technogym.
Sit on the machine and set the rest position to a comfortable opening angle.
Close your legs.
Gently return to the rest position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2492','CC-BY-SA 4','lbroggi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2493','Adductor Side Plank','Adductor Side Plank','Set up next to a bench in a  90° angle on your side. One leg goes up on the bench with the side of your calf touching it. The other leg goes below the bench. Forearm closer to the ground is at a 90° angle, hand pointing front. Now push off the floor with the forearm closer to the ground, upper side of your body should be completely straight, level with the bench (it''s a side plank after all). Hold that position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2493','CC-BY-SA 4','hurr99','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2494','Band Terminal Knee extension','Band Terminal Knee extension','This is an end range strengthening exercise for the knee extensors. Start by looping a band around the back of one knee and anchoring the other end to a stable surface in front of you. Stand in a split stance with the banded knee bent and placed as the front leg. Straighten the knee to pull against the bands resistance and maintain a contraction in your quadriceps for up to 5 seconds before releasing.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_2494/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2494','CC-BY-SA 4','Rehab Hero','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2495','Machine Leg Flexion','Machine Leg Flexion','Adjust the back seat or pad so your knees align with the side pivot axis.Place the lower roller pad against your lower calves, just above the back of your ankles.Lower the upper thigh restraint pad so your legs stay firmly on the seat.Pick a light weight on the stack with the pin.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_2495/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2495','CC-BY-SA 4','Me','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2496','Wall Push-ups (Vasco L1)','Wall Push-ups (Vasco L1)','Vasco custom beginner wall push-up for zero-equipment home training. Part of 7-day Push/Pull/Core/Lower/Full/Recovery/Rest periodization. 6:30 AM wake, 1hr sessions. Stoic discipline focus.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2496','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2497','DB Floor Press (5kg Single Arm)','DB Floor Press (5kg Single Arm)','Vasco custom single-arm DB floor press for 5kg dumbbell home training. Unilateral work for symmetry and core anti-rotation. Part of Monday Push day.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2497','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2498','Pike Push-ups (Vasco L1)','Pike Push-ups (Vasco L1)','Vasco custom pike push-up for shoulder development in beginner home training. Bodyweight only. Part of Monday Push day.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2498','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2499','Incline Push-ups (Vasco L2)','Incline Push-ups (Vasco L2)','Vasco custom incline push-up progression for beginner home training. Bridges wall push-ups to floor push-ups. Part of Monday Push day.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2499','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2501','Table Bodyweight Rows (Vasco L1)','Table Bodyweight Rows (Vasco L1)','Vasco custom table bodyweight row for horizontal pulling in home training. Zero equipment except sturdy table. Part of Tuesday Pull day.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2501','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2502','DB Single-Arm Row (5kg)','DB Single-Arm Row (5kg)','Vasco custom single-arm DB row for 5kg dumbbell home training. Unilateral horizontal pull. Part of Tuesday Pull day.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Back','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2502','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2503','Face Pulls (Bodyweight Doorframe/Towel)','Face Pulls (Bodyweight Doorframe/Towel)','Vasco custom face pull variation using doorframe or towel for rear delt development. Zero equipment. Part of Tuesday Pull day.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2503','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2504','DB Hammer Curls (5kg)','DB Hammer Curls (5kg)','Vasco custom single-arm hammer curl for 5kg dumbbell. Targets brachialis for arm thickness. Part of Tuesday Pull day.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2504','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2505','Dead Bug (Core L1)','Dead Bug (Core L1)','Vasco custom dead bug - foundational deep core stability and anti-extension. Teaches lumbar-pelvic dissociation, breath-coordination, and proximal stability for distal mobility. Prerequisite for all core training.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2505','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2507','Forearm Plank (Core L1)','Forearm Plank (Core L1)','Vasco custom forearm plank - foundational anterior core stability exercise. Teaches full-body tension, breath control, and anti-extension. Prerequisite for all advanced core work.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2507','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2508','Bird Dog (Core L1)','Bird Dog (Core L1)','Vasco custom bird dog - foundational contralateral limb coordination and lumbar stability. Teaches hip dissociation from spine, glute activation, and scapular control.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2508','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2509','Side Plank (Core L1)','Side Plank (Core L1)','Vasco custom side plank - foundational lateral core stability. Targets obliques, QL, and hip abductors. Essential for spinal stability and rotational control.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','BACK','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','lats','chest','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2509','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2510','Hollow Body Hold (Core L1)','Hollow Body Hold (Core L1)','Vasco custom hollow body hold - foundational anti-extension core stability. Teaches global anterior chain tension, breath control under load, and positional awareness for gymnastics/calisthenics.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['calves','glutes','shoulders','biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2510','CC-BY-SA 4','Vasco Custom','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2522','Tricep Pull-Down','Tricep Pull-Down','Secure Band above you.

Stand facing band, with feet hip-width apart.
Bend your knees slightly to engage your core.
Keep your chest up, pin your shoulder blades back, and tuck your elbows tightly to the sides of your torso.
Exhale and pull the band straight down toward your thighs.
Inhale and slowly control the band as you let your arms return upwards to their starting position.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','chest']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2522','CC-BY-SA 4','G. Johnson','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2523','Serratus Wall Slide Stretch','Serratus Wall Slide Stretch','Stand facing a wall. Place your forearms vertically against the wall so your elbows and wrists are both touching it.
Point your arms slightly outwards from "straight up".
Protract your shoulders had, then slide your forearms up the wall until your elbows are about level with your chin.
Slide your forearms back down the wall. Repeat as necessary.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2523','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2524','Straddle Stance Good Morning','Straddle Stance Good Morning','Hold the barbell on your shoulders as if to squat.
Take a half-step forwards with one leg, placing your foot on the ground.
Lock the front leg, and either lock your back leg or allow it to bend very slightly.
Bend forwards under control to stretch the rear of your front leg, then return to your standing position.

Repeat as necessary for reps/time. You should also repeat for the other leg.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2524','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2525','Couch Stretch','Couch Stretch','Stand facing away from a bench, couch or similar-height object.
Extend one leg backwards, resting your foot "laces-down" on the edge of the bench.
Lower yourself until your rear knee is on the floor and you are in a lunge position, with your torso hanging forwards slightly.
Brace your core, tense your rear glute, and straighten up your torso to vertical, under control. Relax and repeat.

Repeat for the other leg, too.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['BENCH']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2525','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2526','Long Lunge Pulse Stretch','Long Lunge Pulse Stretch','Hold the resistance band (or any other rope-like object, the elasticity is not necessary) above your head, between your hands, with your arms straight. Pull it taught to engage your lats.
Step forwards into a lunge, dropping until your knee is almost touching the floor.
Slowly and controlledly pulse your body up and down by about an inch. Repeat for required reps.
Repeat for other leg.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2526','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2527','Front Split Stretch','Front Split Stretch','Start kneeling.
Extend one leg out forwards, fully straightened. Follow with your hips so your back leg begins to unfold.
Carefully lower yourself into the stretch. Do not go beyond your limit.
Hold for the required time.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','quads','calves']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2527','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2528','Squat Sky Reach Stretch','Squat Sky Reach Stretch','Drop into a squat.
Hold one ankle with the opposite hand.
Fold your other arm to your chest.
Staying in the squat and keeping hold of your ankle, twist to turn your chest-hand back/outwards until your elbow is pointing at the sky.
Return to the neutral squatting position with your hand on your chest. Repeat movement as required.

Repeat on both sides.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['lats','chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2528','CC-BY-SA 4','Croak6728','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2529','explosive push ups','explosive push ups','Explosive Push-Ups

Start in a standard push-up position, lower your chest, then explosively push off the ground so your hands leave the floor. Land softly and immediately repeat.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_2529/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2529','CC-BY-SA 4','ege','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2530','Russian Push Ups','Russian Push Ups','Russian Push-Ups

Start in a standard push-up position with your hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Lower your chest toward the floor, then shift your body forward while keeping your chest close to the ground. Extend your arms to return to the starting position, then reverse the movement smoothly. Keep your core tight and maintain controlled movement throughout the exercise.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','CORE','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_2530/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2530','CC-BY-SA 4','ege','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2531','elbow lever','elbow lever','​A calisthenics static balance skill where the entire body is held straight and parallel to the ground, supported by tucking the elbows firmly into the abdomen or pelvic bones.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['core','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2531','CC-BY-SA 4','ege','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_2532','Planche Lean Hold','Planche Lean Hold','A straight-arm calisthenics static hold where you assume a plank position and lean the shoulders as far forward as possible past the wrists with protracted scapulae and a hollow body.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','CHEST','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','chest','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','2532','CC-BY-SA 4','ege','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_254','Front Raises with Plates','Front Raises with Plates','The plate front raise is a variation of the dumbbell front raise where the lifter holds a weight plate between two hands, rather than using a dumbbell, barbell, or other weight. It can provide variety in a shoulder-focused muscle-building workout, or as part of an upper body or full-body circuit.

While standing straight, hold a barbell plate in both hands at the 3 and 9 o''clock positions. Your palms should be facing each other and your arms should be extended and locked with a slight bend at the elbows and the plate should be down near your waist in front of you as far as you can go. Tip: The arms will remain in this position throughout the exercise. This will be your starting position.
Slowly raise the plate as you exhale until it is a little above shoulder level. Hold the contraction for a second. As you inhale, slowly lower the plate back down to the starting position.
Repeat for the recommended amount of repetitions.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','254','CC-BY-SA 3','Marius','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_256','Front Raises','Front Raises','To execute the exercise, the lifter stands with their feet shoulder width apart and weights or resistance handles held by their side with a pronated (overhand) grip.

The movement is to bring the arms up in front of the body to eye level and with only a slight bend in the elbow. This isolates the anterior deltoid muscle (front of the shoulder) and uses the anterior deltoid to lift the weight.

When lifting it is important to keep the body still so the anterior deltoid is fully utilised; if the weight cannot be lifted by standing still then it is too heavy and a lower weight is needed. It is important to keep a slight bend in the elbow when lifting as keeping the elbow locked will add stress to the elbow joint and could cause injury.

A neutral grip, similar to that used in the hammer curl, can also be used. With this variation the weight is again raised to eye level, but out to a 45 degree angle from the front of the body. This may be beneficial for those with shoulder injuries, particularly those related to the rotator cuff.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_256/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','256','CC-BY-SA 3','Manu, wikipedia','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_257','Front Squats','Front Squats','This variation of the squat trains the hamstrings and gluteus maximus. It also works the back extensors and abductors.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_257/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','257','CC-BY-SA 3','sistab2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_258','Front pull wide','Front pull wide',NULL,'BACK',ARRAY['BACK','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','shoulders','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','258','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_259','Front Pull narrow','Front Pull narrow',NULL,'BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','259','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_260','Full Sit Outs','Full Sit Outs','(A) Get in high plank position on your hands and toes.(B) Shift your weight to your left hand as you turn your body to the right; bend your right leg behind you and extend your right arm up. Return to the center and repeat on the opposite side. Continue, alternating sides.Make it easier: Don’t raise your arm after you bend your leg behind you.Make it harder: Balance with your arm and leg extended for two counts.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','260','CC-BY-SA 4','http://www.realsimple.com/health/fitness-exercise/','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_265','Glute Bridge','Glute Bridge','Lie on you back with your hips and knees flexed, feet on the ground. From this position, raise your butt off of the ground to a height where your body makes a straight line from your knees to your shoulders. To make the exercise more intense, you can add weight by letting a barbell rest on your hips as you complete the motion, or you can put your feet on a slightly higher surface such as a step or a bench.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','265','CC-BY-SA 4','tdprice12','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_272','Hammer Curls','Hammer Curls','Start: Hold dumbbells at your sides with palms facing your torso.
Curl: Lift the weights toward your shoulders while maintaining the neutral grip (like holding a hammer).
Squeeze: Contract the biceps at the top without moving your elbows forward.
Lower: Slowly return to the starting position with full control.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_272/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','272','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_275','Hammercurls on Cable','Hammercurls on Cable','Take a cable in your hands (palms parallel, point to each other), the body is straight. Bend the arms and bring the weight up with a fast movement. Without any pause bring it back down with a slow, controlled movement, but don''t stretch completely your arms.

Don''t swing your body during the exercise, the biceps should do all the work here. The elbows are at your side and don''t move.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_275/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','275','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_279','Hand Grip','Hand Grip','chrome Hand Flex Grip to build up forearms muscles','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_279/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','279','CC-BY-SA 4','vince63','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_282','Handstand Pushup','Handstand Pushup','The handstand push-up (press-up) - also called the vertical push-up (press-up) or the inverted push-up (press-up) also called commandos- is a type of push-up exercise where the body is positioned in a handstand. For a true handstand, the exercise is performed free-standing, held in the air. To prepare the strength until one has built adequate balance, the feet are often placed against a wall, held by a partner, or secured in some other way from falling. Handstand pushups require significant strength, as well as balance and control if performed free-standing.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_282/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','282','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_283','Hanging Leg Raises','Hanging Leg Raises','Hanging from bar or straps, bring legs up with knees extended or flexed','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','283','CC-BY-SA 3','robhoyt','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_284','Hercules Pillars','Hercules Pillars','Grab two cables stand in the middle so both have tension and hold','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','triceps','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','284','CC-BY-SA 3','GrosseHund','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_285','High Knee Jumps','High Knee Jumps','Start with legs slightly wider than shoulder width
Drop into a bodyweight squat
As you hit the bottom of the squat, explode upwards into a jump while simultaneously tucking your knees into your chest midflight.  Remain tucked until the apex of your jump.
Land on both feet, making sure your knees are not locked so as to avoid excessive strain upon your joints.  Collect yourself into the next rep as quickly but under control as possible.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','calves','quads','core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_285/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','285','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_289','High Pull','High Pull','Use a light barbell, perform explosive lift up starting from underneath knee cap level. Lift/raise explosively using hips, at shoulder level. Tempo: 2111','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','289','CC-BY-SA 3','Mahoney','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_291','Hindu Squats','Hindu Squats','Start with your feet shoulder width apart and arms slightly behind your back.

As you descend towards the floor, raise your heels off the ground, while keeping your back as vertical  as possible.

Upon attaining the bottom position, touch the hands to the heels.

Then stand up ending with the heels on the ground, arms extended in front of the chest then rowing into the start position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','291','CC-BY-SA 4','Vilhelmo','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_292','Hip Raise, Lying','Hip Raise, Lying','Lying down on your back, with your feet flat on the floor. Raise your hips up evenly as high as you can and hold for as long as you can.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','292','CC-BY-SA 4','James Mackay','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_294','Hip Thrust','Hip Thrust','The bar should go directly on your upper thigh, directly below your crotch. Your feet should be directly under your knees. Push your hips up so that you form a straight line from your knees to your shoulders. Use a pad for comfort.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','294','CC-BY-SA 4','Bret Contreras','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_297','Hollow Hold','Hollow Hold','Get on a mat and lie on your back. Contract your abs, stretch your arms and legs and raise them (your head and shoulders are also be raised). Make sure your lower back remains in contact with the mat.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_297/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','297','CC0','Behrooz','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_301','Hyperextensions','Hyperextensions','Lie on the hyperextension pillow with your navel at the front edge, allowing your upper body to hang freely. Tighten all your back muscles and raise your torso until you''re horizontal, but no higher. Lower yourself slowly, maintaining a steady flow of muscles.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_301/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','301','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_308','Incline Dumbbell Fly','Incline Dumbbell Fly','Use inclined bench. Hold dumbbells straight out to your sides, elbows slightly bent. Bring arms together above you, keeping angle of elbows fixed.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','308','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_31','Axe Hold','Axe Hold','Grab dumbbells and extend arms to side and hold as long as you can','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_31/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','31','CC-BY-SA 3','GrosseHund','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_310','Incline Dumbbell Row','Incline Dumbbell Row','Using a neutral grip, lean into an incline bench.
Take a dumbbell in each hand with a neutral grip, beginning with the arms straight. This will be your starting position.
Retract the shoulder blades and flex the elbows to row the dumbbells to your side.
Pause at the top of the motion, and then return to the starting position.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','310','CC-BY-SA 4','cal.zabel','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_312','Incline Plank With Alternate Floor Touch','Incline Plank With Alternate Floor Touch','Perform the plank with legs elevated, feet on a gymball. Once stabilised, slowly move one foot sideways off the ball, then make it touch the floor, then come back to starting position. Alternate with the other foot.

This is a core exercise.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','312','CC-BY-SA 3','Mahoney','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_314','Isometric Wipers','Isometric Wipers','Assume push-up position, with hands slightly wider than shoulder width.

Shift body weight as far as possible to one side, allowing the elbow on that side to flex.

Reverse the motion, moving completely over to the other side.

Return to the starting position, and repeat for the desired number of repetitions.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['chest','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','314','CC-BY-SA 4','cal.zabel','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_319','Jogging','Jogging','Get your shoes on, go outside and start running at a moderate pace.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','319','CC-BY-SA 4','Papazit','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_320','Jumping Jacks','Jumping Jacks','A jumping jack or star jump, also called side-straddle hop in the US military, is a physical jumping exercise performed by jumping to a position with the legs spread wide and the hands going overhead, sometimes in a clap, and then returning to a position with the feet together and the arms at the sides','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_320/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','320','CC-BY-SA 4','student1234','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_323','Cable Cross-over','Cable Cross-over','Begin with cables at about shoulder height, one in each hand. Take a step forward so that one foot is in front of the other, for stability, and so that there is tension on the cables. Bring hands together in front of you. Try to make your hands overlap (so that the cables cross) a few inches.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_323/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','323','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_331','Kettlebell Swings','Kettlebell Swings','Hold the kettlebell securely in both hands. Keep your back flat throughout the move, avoiding any rounding of the spine.Keeping your knees "soft", hinge your hips backwards, letting the kettlebell swing between your knees.

You want to bend from the hips as far as you can without letting your back round forwards. Then, snap your hips forwards quickly and standing up straight, locking your body in an upright posture.

The speed you do this will cause your arms and the kettlebell to swing up in front of you. Don''t try to lift the kettlebell with your arms. The snapping forwards of your hips will cause the kettlebell to swing forwards through momentum. Depending on the weight of the kettlebell and the speed of your hip movement, your arms will swing up to about shoulder height. At the top of this swing, let your hips hinge backwards again as the kettlebell swings back down to between your legs and the start of the next repetition.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','hamstrings']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','331','CC-BY-SA 3','J120290,cerin','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_341','Squats on Multipress','Squats on Multipress',NULL,'LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','341','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_346','Landmine press','Landmine press',NULL,'SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','346','CC-BY-SA 4','Torsten Linnecke','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_348','Lateral Raises','Lateral Raises','This exercise works the deltoid muscle of the shoulder. The movement starts with the arms straight, and the hands holding weights at the sides or in front of the body. Body is in a slight forward-leaning position with hips and knees bent a little. Arms are kept straight or slightly bent, and raised through an arc of movement in the coronal plane that terminates when the hands are at approximately shoulder height. Weights are lowered to the starting position, completing one rep. When using a cable machine the individual stands with the coronal plane in line with the pulley, which is at or near the ground.[9] The exercise can be completed one shoulder at a time (with the other hand used to stabilize the body against the weight moved), or with both hands simultaneously if two parallel pulleys are available.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_348/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','348','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_349','Lateral Rows on Cable, One Armed','Lateral Rows on Cable, One Armed','Set cable at waist height, start with arm across your belly and move han over and out too other side, one arm at the time.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_349/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','349','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_351','Lateral-to-Front Raises','Lateral-to-Front Raises','-(1) Perform a lateral raise, pausing at the top of the lift (2).

-Instead of lowering the weight, bring it to the front of your body so that you appear to be at the top position of a front raise.  You will do this by using a Pec Fly motion, maintaining straight arms. (3)

-Now lower the weight to your quadriceps, or, in other words, lower the dumbbells as though you are completing a Front Raise repetition. (4)

-Reverse the motion:  Perform a front raise (5), at the apex of the lift use a Reverse Fly motion to position the weights at the top of a Lateral Raise (6), and finally, lower the weights until your palms are essentially touching the sides of your thighs (7).  THIS IS ONE REP.

(1) l  front view(2) -l-  FV  (3) l-  side view   (4) l  SV/FV   (5) l-  SV (6) -l-  FV  (7)  l  FV/SV','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','351','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_354','Lat Pull Down (Leaning Back)','Lat Pull Down (Leaning Back)','Lean Back, Pull into chest','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','354','CC-BY-SA 3','drthurlow','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_355','Lat Pull Down (Straight Back)','Lat Pull Down (Straight Back)','The lat pull down is an exercise used to build the muscles of the back. While the exercise will primarily target the lats, you will also notice a fair amount of bicep and middle back activation.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','355','CC-BY-SA 3','drthurlow','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_364','Leg Curl','Leg Curl','The leg curl, also known as the hamstring curl, is an isolation exercise that targets the hamstring muscles. The exercise involves flexing the lower leg against resistance towards the buttocks. Other exercises that can be used to strengthen the hamstrings are the glute-ham raise and the deadlift.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_364/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','364','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_365','Leg Curls (laying)','Leg Curls (laying)','Lay on a bench and put your calves behind the leg holder (better if they are hold on around the lower calves). Hold a grip on the bars to make sure the body is firmly in place. Bend your legs bringing the weight up, go slowly back. During the exercise the body should not move, all work is done by the legs.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_365/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','365','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_366','Leg Curls (sitting)','Leg Curls (sitting)',NULL,'LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_366/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','366','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_367','Leg Curls (standing)','Leg Curls (standing)',NULL,'LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_367/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','367','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_369','Leg Extension','Leg Extension','The leg extension is a resistance weight training exercise that targets the quadriceps muscle in the legs. The exercise is done using a machine called the Leg Extension Machine. There are various manufacturers of these machines and each one is slightly different. Most gym and weight rooms will have the machine in their facility. The leg extension is an isolated exercise targeting one specific muscle group, the quadriceps. It should not be considered as a total leg workout, such as the squat or deadlift. The exercise consists of bending the leg at the knee and extending the legs, then lowering them back to the original position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_369/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','369','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_371','Leg Press','Leg Press','The leg press is a weight training exercise in which the individual pushes a weight or resistance away from them using their legs.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','calves','glutes','quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_371/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','371','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_373','Leg Presses (narrow)','Leg Presses (narrow)','The exercise is very similar to the wide leg press:

Sit on the machine and put your feet on the platform so far apart  that you could just put another foot in between them. The feet are parallel and point up.

Lower the weight so much, that the knees form a right angle. Push immediately the platform up again, without any pause. When in the lower position, the knees point a bit outwards and the movement should be always fluid.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_373/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','373','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_374','Leg Presses (wide)','Leg Presses (wide)','Sit on the machine and put your feet on the platform, a bit more than shoulder wide. The feet are turned outwards by a few degrees.

Lower the weight so much, that the knees form a right angle. Push immediately the platform up again, without any pause. When in the lower position, the knees point a bit outwards and the movement should be always fluid.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','374','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_375','Leg Press on Hackenschmidt Machine','Leg Press on Hackenschmidt Machine',NULL,'LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_375/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','375','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_376','Leg Raise','Leg Raise','The leg raise is a strength training exercise which targets the iliopsoas (the anterior hip flexors). Because the abdominal muscles are used isometrically to stabilize the body during the motion, leg raises are also often used to strengthen the rectus abdominis muscle and the internal and external oblique muscles.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','376','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_377','Leg Raises, Lying','Leg Raises, Lying','Lay down on a bench and hold onto the recliner with your hands to keep you stable. Hold your legs straight and lift them till they make an angle of about 45°. Make a short pause of 1 sec. and go slowly down to the initial position. To increase the intensity you can make a longer pause of 7 sec. every 5th time.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_377/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','377','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_378','Leg Raises, Standing','Leg Raises, Standing','Put your forearms on the pads on the leg raise machine, the body is hanging freely. Lift now your legs with a fast movement as high as you can, make a short pause of 1sec at the top, and bring them down again. Make sure that during the exercise your body does not swing, only the legs should move.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','378','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_379','Leverage Machine Chest Press','Leverage Machine Chest Press','Be sure to adjust seat height so that the handles are towards the bottom of your pectorals.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','379','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_380','Leverage Machine Iso Row','Leverage Machine Iso Row','Adjust seat height so that the handles are at the bottom of your pectorals or just below.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','380','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_382','L Hold','L Hold','Hold the L position for as long as possible','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','382','CC-BY-SA 3','bizyguy','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_386','Diamond push ups','Diamond push ups','Start: Get into a plank. Place hands close together under your chest so thumbs and index fingers form a diamond shape.

Lower: Bend your elbows to lower your chest toward your hands. Keep your body straight.

Push: Push back up until arms are fully extended.

New note Keep elbows close to your body and core tight.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','386','CC-BY-SA 4','notdefine','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_394','Long-Pulley (low Row)','Long-Pulley (low Row)','Sit down, put your feet on the supporting points and grab the bar with a wide grip. Pull the weight with a rapid movement towards your belly button, not upper. Keep your arms and elbows during the movement close to your body. Your shoulders are pulled together. Let the weight slowly down till your arms are completely stretched.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_394/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','394','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_395','Long-Pulley, Narrow','Long-Pulley, Narrow','The exercise is the same as the regular long pulley, but with a narrow grip:

Sit down, put your feet on the supporting points and grab the bar with a wide grip. Pull the weight with a rapid movement towards your belly button, not upper. Keep your arms and elbows during the movement close to your body. Your shoulders are pulled together. Let the weight slowly down till your arms are completely stretched.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','395','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_397','Low Box Squat - Wide Stance','Low Box Squat - Wide Stance','Unrack the bar and set your stance wide, beyond your hips.  Push your hips back and sit down to a box that takes you below parallel.  Sit completely down, do not touch and go.  Then explosively stand up.  Stay tight in your upper back and torso throughout the movement.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','397','CC-BY-SA 4','taylorbarbell','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_406','Lying Rotator Cuff Exercise','Lying Rotator Cuff Exercise','This is an excercise for problems with the rotator cuff. Primary  Infraspinatus, secondary Teres Minor.

Lying on side. Keep elbow on waist and in 90 dgr angle. Rotate towards stomach. Add weight as fit.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','406','CC-BY-SA 4','Trix','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_41','Barbell Ab Rollout','Barbell Ab Rollout','Place a barbell on the floor at your feet.

Bending at the waist, grip the barbell with a shoulder with overhand grip.

With a slow controlled motion, roll the bar out so that your back is straight.

Roll back up raising your hips and butt as you return to the starting position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_41/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','41','CC-BY-SA 4','sevae','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_418','Military Press mit SZ-Bar','Military Press mit SZ-Bar','On an SZ-bar grip your hands on the outside of each bend and stand with your arms straight down, palms facing your legs. Pull the bar (bending your arms at the elbow) to your chest, and the push the bar above your head (arms as straight as possible). Return the bar to your chest by dropping your arms at the elbows. Return the bar to it''s origional position (stand with your arms straight down, palms facing your legs.)','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_418/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','418','CC-BY-SA 3','mbozi1','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_423','Muscle up','Muscle up','The body is then explosively pulled up by the arms in a radial pull-up, with greater speed than a regular pull-up. When the bar approaches the upper chest, the wrists are swiftly flexed to bring the forearms above the bar. The body is leaned forward, and the elbows are straightened by activating the triceps. The routine is considered complete when the bar is at the level of the waist and the arms are fully straight.

To dismount, the arms are bent at the elbow, and the body is lowered to the floor, and the exercise can be repeated.

As a relatively advanced exercise, muscle-ups are typically first learned with an assistive kip. The legs swing (kip) up and provide momentum to assist in the explosive upward force needed to ascend above the bar. More advanced athletes can perform a strict variation of the muscle-up which is done slowly, without any kip. This variation begins with a still dead hang and uses isometric muscle contraction to ascend above the bar in a slow, controlled fashion.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','BACK','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps','lats','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','423','CC-BY-SA 4','arson','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_427','Negative Crunches','Negative Crunches','Sit yourself on the decline bench and fix your legs. Cross your arms over the chest and bring with a rolling movement your upper body up, go now without a pause and with a slow movement down again. Don''t let your head move during the exercise.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_427/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','427','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_43','Barbell Hack Squats','Barbell Hack Squats','Perform leg squats with barbell behind your legs','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','43','CC-BY-SA 4','BePieToday','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_439','Overhand Cable Curl','Overhand Cable Curl','Hands at shoulder height, curl arms in toward head, then back out.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','439','CC-BY-SA 3','ThisGirl0819','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_441','Overhead Squat','Overhead Squat','The barbell is held overhead in a wide-arm snatch grip; however, it is also possible to use a closer grip if balance allows.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','shoulders','hamstrings']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','441','CC-BY-SA 4','geraldbaeck','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_445','Pause Bench','Pause Bench','Lower the bar to your chest and pause (but do not rest) there for 2 seconds. Press back up. use the same weight you would on bench press, but perform only single reps. Total the number of reps you did in one set of bench press (if you did 3 sets of 8 do 8 sinlge pause bench reps.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','445','CC0','Mens Fitness','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_448','Pendelay Rows','Pendelay Rows','Back excercise with a barbell with a starting position which is in a bent over position with the back paralell to the ground. The barbell is on the ground at chest level.For the movement grab the barbell at shoulder width grip and pull towards your chest without losing the bent over position and without moving anything but your arms','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','448','CC-BY-SA 3','Nallitnas','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_454','Pike Push Ups','Pike Push Ups','Push Up performed from a pike position (optional to have feet elevated).','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_454/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','454','CC-BY-SA 4','Nash','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_456','Pistol Squat','Pistol Squat','Stand with feet hip-width apart, toes pointed forward, and chest tall.
Extend your leg straight out; extend both arms in front of you, at shoulder level. Brace your core and look straight ahead.
Slowly squat down.
(optional) pause at the bottom.

Keep your (free) leg and arms extended for the whole duration.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','shoulders','biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_456/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','456','CC-BY-SA 3','minifigmaster125','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_458','Plank','Plank','Get into a position on the floor supporting your weight on your forearms and toes. Arms are bent and directly below the shoulder.

Keep your body straight at all times and hold this position as long as possible. To increase difficulty an arm or leg can be raised while performing this exercise.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE','ARMS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['core','biceps','quads','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_458/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','458','CC-BY-SA 3','YYCfit / BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_46','Barbell Lunges Standing','Barbell Lunges Standing','Put barbell on the back of your shoulders. Stand upright, then take the first step forward. Step should bring you forward so that your supporting legs knee can touch the floor. Then stand back up and repeat with the other leg.

Remember to keep good posture.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','46','CC-BY-SA 4','Mikko Ruohola','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_465','Preacher Curls','Preacher Curls','Place the EZ curl bar on the rest handles in front of the preacher bench. Lean over the bench and grab the EZ curl bar with palms up. Sit down on the preacher bench seat so your upper arms rest on top of the pad and your chest is pressed against the pad. Lower the weight until your elbows are extended and arms are straight. Bring the weights back up to the starting point by contracting biceps. Repeat','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_465/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','465','CC-BY-SA 3','cgoob883','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_468','Prone Scapular Retraction - Arms at Side','Prone Scapular Retraction - Arms at Side','Lying on stomach with head on towel.

Stretch arms straight out to your sides.

Slowly lift your arms, pulling your shoulderblades together, hold for 3 seconds.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','468','CC-BY-SA 4','donaddon','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_475','Pull-ups','Pull-ups','Grab the pull up bar with a wide grip, the body is hanging freely. Keep your chest out and pull yourself up till your chin reaches the bar or it touches your neck, if you want to pull behind you. Go with a slow and controlled movement down, always keeping the chest out.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','shoulders','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_475/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','475','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
