('wger_505','Roman Chair Crunch','Roman Chair Crunch','Crunches on roman chair. Keep your torso straight, abs tight, and don''t come up all the way vertical or lie flat to keep constant tension on your abs.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','505','CC-BY-SA 3','MaddieBeasley','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_507','Romanian Deadlift','Romanian Deadlift','DL from top to pos 2: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WtWtjViRsKo','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','507','CC-BY-SA 4','pjwirth','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_508','Row','Row','In strength training, rowing (or a row, usually preceded by a qualifying adjective — for instance a seated row) is an exercise where the purpose is to strengthen the muscles that draw the rower''s arms toward the body (latissimus dorsi) as well as those that retract the scapulae (trapezius and rhomboids) and those that support the spine (erector spinae). When done on a rowing machine, rowing also exercises muscles that extend and support the legs (quadriceps and thigh muscles). In all cases, the abdominal and lower back muscles must be used in order to support the body and prevent back injury.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','quads']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','DUMBBELL','PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','508','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_51','Barbell Wrist Curl','Barbell Wrist Curl','Sitting on a bench, grab a barbell with your palms facing up and your hands shoulder-width apart. Rest your forearms on your thighs and allow your wrists to hang over your knees. Perform the movement by curling your palms and wrists towards your face.

Pause for a moment in the top position, then slowly return the barbell to the starting position.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_51/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','51','CC-BY-SA 4','burenl','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
