('wger_512','Rowing seated, narrow grip','Rowing seated, narrow grip','Tighten muscles
Controlled movement
Slow movement
Keep upper body upright
Do not lean back
Pull toward chest','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_512/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','512','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_513','Rowing, T-bar','Rowing, T-bar','The execution of this exercise is very similar to the regular bent over rowing, only that the bar is fixed here.

Grab the barbell with a wide grip (slightly more than shoulder wide) and lean forward. Your upper body is not quite parallel to the floor, but forms a slight angle. The chest''s out during the whole exercise. Pull now the barbell with a fast movement towards your belly button, not further up. Go slowly down to the initial position. Don''t swing with your body and keep your arms next to your body.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','shoulders','biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_513/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','513','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
