('wger_537','Incline Bench Press - Dumbbell','Incline Bench Press - Dumbbell','This is a variation of the flat bench press designed to emphasize the clavicular head of the pectoralis major (the upper portion). By tilting the torso, the angle of the push changes, shifting more tension to the upper chest and shoulders, which helps achieve a more aesthetic, balanced, and three-dimensional development of the torso.

Bench Adjustment and Preparation: Set the bench to an incline of between 30 and 45 degrees (an incline greater than 45° will place too much strain on the shoulders and reduce the stimulus to the chest). Sit down with a dumbbell on each thigh.

Starting position: Lean back, resting your back against the bench, while using your knees one after the other to push the dumbbells upward to shoulder height.

Anatomical Stabilization: Plant your feet firmly on the floor. Retract your scapulas (bring your shoulder blades together and press them into the bench) to protect your shoulders and stabilize the load.

Eccentric Phase (Lowering): Lower the dumbbells slowly and in a controlled manner toward the upper part of your chest. Your elbows should not splay out to the sides (90°); maintain a safe angle of about 45 to 60 degrees relative to your torso.

Concentric Phase (Lift): Push the dumbbells vertically upward as you exhale. Follow a slightly converging path (without letting them touch at the top). Stop the movement just before locking out your elbows to maintain muscle tension in the upper pectoral.','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_537/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','537','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_538','Incline Bench Press - Barbell','Incline Bench Press - Barbell','To do slowly, tempo is 4010','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_538/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','538','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
