('wger_543','Shoulder Press, on Machine','Shoulder Press, on Machine',NULL,'SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_543/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','543','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_545','Scissors','Scissors','Scissors is an abdominal exercise that strengthens the transverse abdominals, helping flatten your belly and strengthen your entire core. Scissors is not only a core strength move, but it is also a great stretch for your hamstrings and your lower back. Everyone is looking for new ways to work the core, to flatten the belly and to improve flexibility. If you learn how to do Scissors you will get everything rolled together in one move.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','545','CC-BY-SA 4','vkylamba','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_549','Seated Triceps Press','Seated Triceps Press','Sit down on a back (better with back support). Take a dumbbell firmly with both hands and hold it with extended arms over your head. With your palms facing upward and holding the weight of the dumbbell, slowly lower the weight behind your head.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','549','CC-BY-SA 4','richmr2174@gmail.com','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_556','Side Bends on Machine','Side Bends on Machine',NULL,'CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','556','CC-BY-SA 3','klabautermann','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_56','Abdominal Stabilization','Abdominal Stabilization',NULL,'CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','56','CC-BY-SA 3','andikeller','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_562','Shotgun Row','Shotgun Row','Attach a single handle to a low cable.
After selecting the correct weight, stand a couple feet back with a wide-split stance. Your arm should be extended and your shoulder forward. This will be your starting position.
Perform the movement by retracting the shoulder and flexing the elbow. As you pull, supinate the wrist, turning the palm upward as you go.
After a brief pause, return to the starting position.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','562','CC-BY-SA 4','cal.zabel','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_566','Shoulder Press, Barbell','Shoulder Press, Barbell','Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a barbell with a shoulder wide grip and bring it up to chest height. Press the weight up, but don''t stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_566/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','566','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_567','Shoulder Press, Dumbbells','Shoulder Press, Dumbbells','Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take two dumbbells and bring them up to shoulder height, the palms and the elbows point during the whole exercise to the front. Press the weights up, at the highest point they come very near but don''t touch. Go slowly down and repeat.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_567/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','567','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_569','Shoulder Press, on Multi Press','Shoulder Press, on Multi Press','The exercise is basically the same as with a free barbell:

Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a bar with a shoulder wide grip and bring it down to chest height. Press the weight up, but don''t stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','569','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_57','Bear Walk 2','Bear Walk 2','-Rest your weight on your palms and the balls of your feet, not dissimilar to normal pushup position

-Move by stepping with your R palm and L foot, then your L palm and R foot.  Basically, walk like a lumbering bear.

-Move as fast as you can.  Measure your reps/sets in either distance (i.e. 40 yards) or time (i.e. 45 seconds)

-Works your Pecs, Deltoids, Triceps, Traps, Lats, Abs and Lower Back, Hip Flexors, Quads, Glutes and Calves','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','CHEST','CORE','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','calves','chest','core','triceps','glutes','lats','quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','57','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_570','Shoulder Shrug','Shoulder Shrug','The shoulder shrug (usually called simply the shrug) is an exercise in weight training used to develop the upper trapezius muscle. The lifter stands erect, hands about shoulder width apart, and raises the shoulders as high as possible, and then lowers them, while not bending the elbows, or moving the body at all. The lifter may not have as large a range of motion as in a normal shrug done for active flexibility. It is usually considered good form if the slope of the shoulders is horizontal in the elevated position.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_570/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','570','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_571','Shrugs, Barbells','Shrugs, Barbells','Take a barbell and stand with a straight body, the arms are hanging freely in front of you. Lift from this position the shoulders as high as you can, but don''t bend the arms during the movement. On the highest point, make a short pause of 1 or 2 seconds before returning slowly to the initial position.

When training with a higher weight, make sure that you still do the whole movement!','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_571/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','571','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_572','Shrugs, Dumbbells','Shrugs, Dumbbells','Stand with straight body, the hands are hanging freely on the side and hold each a dumbbell. Lift from this position the shoulders as high as you can, but don''t bend the arms during the movement. On the highest point, make a short pause of 1 or 2 seconds before returning slowly to the initial position.

When training with a higher weight, make sure that you still do the whole movement!','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_572/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','572','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_575','Shrugs on Multipress','Shrugs on Multipress',NULL,'SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','575','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_576','Side Crunch','Side Crunch','Hold weight in one hand. Bend side ways to the knee. Pull upo to upright position using your obliquus.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_576/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','576','CC-BY-SA 3','kwrindy','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_577','Side Dumbbell Trunk Flexion','Side Dumbbell Trunk Flexion','AKA dumbbell side bends. Stand in line with the hips with slightly bent knees, maintain the natural curvature of the spine, hand stretched by the body, grip the barbell with one hand. Make slow and controlled torso side flexions till you reach the angle of approximately 45°.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','577','CC-BY-SA 3','GiglioRosso','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_578','Side-lying External Rotation','Side-lying External Rotation','With a weight in one hand, lie on your side opposite the weight. Keep your knees slightly bent. Hold your elbow against your side, and extend your upper arm straight ahead of you. While continuing to hold your elbow against your side, rotate your upper arm 90 degrees upwards.

It is helpful to place a towel under your armpit to help with the form on this exercise. Placing a support under your head for the duration of the exercise is also a good idea.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','578','CC-BY-SA 4','apeschel','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_580','Side Plank','Side Plank','Works your obliques and helps stabilize your spine. Lie on your side and support your body between your forearm and knee to your feet.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','580','CC-BY-SA 4','http://www.bodybuilding.com/','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_583','Side to Side Push Ups','Side to Side Push Ups','-start in push up position

-lean the body weight to the right side, and complete a push up with the chest over the right hand

-come back to the centered position

-on rep 2, lean to the left side','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','CHEST','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','chest','triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','583','CC-BY-SA 4','nate303303','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_584','Single-arm Preacher Curl','Single-arm Preacher Curl','Sit on the preacher curl bench and perform a bicep curl with a dumbbell in one hand. Your other hand can be at rest, or beneath your curling arm''s elbow.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms','unilateral',NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','584','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_590','Sitting Calf Raises','Sitting Calf Raises','Sit on a bench for calf raises and check that the feet are half free and that you can completely stretch the calf muscles down. Pull your calves up, going as far (up) as you can. Make at the highest point a short pause of 1 or 2 seconds and go down.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Calves',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','590','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_591','Sit-ups','Sit-ups','Sit on a mat, your calves are resting on a bench, the knees make a right angle. Hold your hands behind your neck. Go now up with a rolling movement of your back, you should feel how the individual vertebrae lose contact with the mat. At the highest point, contract your abs as much as you can and hold there for 2 sec. Go now down, unrolling your back.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','591','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_595','Skipping - Standard','Skipping - Standard','Do a single, double footed jump for each swing of the rope.

Work on a smooth, rhythmical movement, bouncing lightly on the balls of your feet.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','595','CC-BY-SA 4','Cerin','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_598','Smith Machine Close-grip Bench Press','Smith Machine Close-grip Bench Press','Perform a standard bench press on the smith machine, but have your hands on the bar about shoulder width apart, and keep your elbows close to your body.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','chest']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','598','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_599','Snatch','Snatch','Stand with your feet at hip width and your shins against the bar. Grasp the bar at double shoulder width and, keeping your lower back flat, drive your heels into the floor to begin lifting the bar. When it''s above your knees, explosively extend your hips and shrug your shoulders. Let the momentum carry the weight overhead.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','599','CC0','Mens Fitness','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_604','Speed Deadlift','Speed Deadlift','Deadlift with short (less than one 1min) rest between sets.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','604','CC-BY-SA 4','MrSteele','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_607','Splinter Sit-ups','Splinter Sit-ups','Lie on your back with your legs straight and arms at your sides, keeping your elbows bent at 90 degrees. As you sit up, twist your upper body to the right and bring your left knee toward your right elbow while you swing your left arm back. Lower your body to the starting position, and repeat to your right. That''s 1 rep.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','607','CC-BY-SA 3','djblitzd','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_614','Squat Jumps','Squat Jumps','Jump wide, then close','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','614','CC-BY-SA 3','OGhTebfCxhexZXuf35mUxV9C--A','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_615','Squats','Squats','Place a barbell in a rack just below shoulder-height. Dip under the bar to put it behind the neck across the top of the back, and grip the bar with the hands wider than shoulder-width apart. Lift the chest up and squeeze the shoulder blades together to keep the straight back throughout the entire movement. Stand up to bring the bar off the rack and step backwards, then place the feet so that they are a little wider than shoulder-width apart. Sit back into hips and keep the back straight and the chest up, squatting down so the hips are below the knees. From the bottom of the squat, press feet into the ground and push hips forward to return to the top of the standing position.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['quads','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','615','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_616','Squat Thrust','Squat Thrust','The burpee, or squat thrust, is a full body exercise used in strength training and as an aerobic exercise. The basic movement is performed in four steps and known as a four-count burpee: Begin in a standing position. Move into a squat position with your hands on the ground. (count 1) Kick your feet back into a plank position, while keeping your arms extended. (count 2) Immediately return your feet into squat position. (count 3) Stand up from the squat position (count 4)','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','616','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_621','Standing Bicep Curl','Standing Bicep Curl','Stand holding dumbbells at shoulder width apart. Face forearm upward and keep upper arm still while raising each dumbbell up to your shoulder.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','621','CC0','BFad07','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_622','Standing Calf Raises','Standing Calf Raises','Get onto the calf raises machine, you should able to completely push your calves down. Stand straight, don''t make a hollow back and don''t bend your legs. Pull yourself up as high as you can. Make a small pause of 1 - 2 seconds and go slowly down.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['calves']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Calves',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_622/0.jpeg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','622','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_623','Standing Rope Forearm','Standing Rope Forearm','Grab a wrist roller tool with both hands while standing with your feet about shoulder width apart. If your gym does not have a wrist roller tool, you can easily put one together. All you need is a 5 or 10 pound weight plate, a strong thin rope about 3 feet long and a 6-8 inch stick or bar. Securely fasten the rope to the middle of the bar/stick and tie the other end of the rope to the weight plate. To begin this exercise, grab the bar/stick with both hands using an overhand grip. Extend both arms straight out in front of you, parallel to the floor. Next, roll the weight up from the floor by rapidly twisting the bar/stick with your hands and wrists. Once the weight reaches the top, slowly lower the plate back to the floor by reversing the motion of your hands and wrists. Repeat (if you can!).','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','623','CC-BY-SA 4','pwiltrout','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_624','Stationary Bike','Stationary Bike','Ride a Stationary Bike with various tensions.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','624','CC-BY-SA 4','intelman','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_627','Stiff-legged Deadlifts','Stiff-legged Deadlifts','Keep legs straight
Keep back straight','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','627','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_628','Straight-arm Pull Down (bar Attachment)','Straight-arm Pull Down (bar Attachment)','Use the straight bar attachment on a high pulley. Grasp the two ends of the bar with your palms facing downward and your arms straight out in front of you. Pull your hands down towards your hips, while keeping your arms straight, then raise them back up to the starting position.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','628','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_629','Straight-arm Pull Down (rope Attachment)','Straight-arm Pull Down (rope Attachment)','Use the rope attachment on a high pulley. Grasp the two ends of the rope with your arms straight out in front of you. Pull your hands down towards your hips, while keeping your arms straight, then raise them back up to the starting position.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','629','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_630','Sumo Deadlift','Sumo Deadlift','Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the shoulders, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the shoulders, which in effect lengthens your arms.
Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your chest up. Drive through the floor, spreading your feet apart, with your weight on the back half of your feet. Extend through the hips and knees.
As the bar passes through the knees, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your shoulder blades together.
Return the weight to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the weight on the way down.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['hamstrings','glutes','quads']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_630/0.webp',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','630','CC-BY-SA 4','magdy','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_632','Sumo Squats','Sumo Squats','Stand with your feet wider than your shoulders, with your toes pointed out at a 45 degree angle and barbell on your shoulder.

While keeping your back straight, descend slowly by bending at the knees and hips as if you are sitting down (squatting).

Lower yourself until your quadriceps and hamstrings are parallel to the floor.

Return to the starting position by pressing upwards and extending your legs while maintaining an equal distribution of weight on your forefoot and heel.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','632','CC-BY-SA 4','sophialj','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_636','Superman','Superman','Lay flat on your stomach with your arms extended in front of you on the ground as your legs are lying flat. Lift both your arms and legs at the same time, as if you were flying, and contract the lower back. Make sure that you are breathing and, depending on your fitness level, hold the movement for at least two to five seconds per repetition.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','636','CC-BY-SA 4','baldurmen','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_650','Thruster','Thruster','Start by doing a front squat
At the top position, push the bar above your head (similar to a press)
Lower the bar to the shoulders','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','650','CC0','BeLikeWater','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_655','Tricep Dumbbell Kickback','Tricep Dumbbell Kickback','Start with a dumbbell in each hand and your palms facing your torso. Keep your back straight with a slight bend in the knees and bend forward at the waist. Your torso should be almost parallel to the floor. Make sure to keep your head up. Your upper arms should be close to your torso and parallel to the floor. Your forearms should be pointed towards the floor as you hold the weights. There should be a 90-degree angle formed between your forearm and upper arm. This is your starting position.
Now, while keeping your upper arms stationary, exhale and use your triceps to lift the weights until the arm is fully extended. Focus on moving the forearm.
After a brief pause at the top contraction, inhale and slowly lower the dumbbells back down to the starting position.
Repeat the movement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.

Variations: This exercise can be executed also one arm at a time much like the one arm rows are performed.

Also, if you like the one arm variety, you can use a low pulley handle instead of a dumbbell for better peak contraction. In this case, the palms should be facing up (supinated grip) as opposed to the torso (neutral grip).','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','655','CC-BY-SA 3','http://www.bodybuilding.com/','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_659','Triceps Extensions on Cable','Triceps Extensions on Cable','Grab the cable, stand with your feet shoulder wide, keep your back straight and lean forward a little. Push the bar down, making sure the elbows don''t move during the exercise. Rotate your hands outwards at the very end and go back to the initial position without pause.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_659/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','659','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_660','Triceps Extensions on Cable With Bar','Triceps Extensions on Cable With Bar','Grab the bar, stand with your feet shoulder wide, keep your back straight and lean forward a little. Push the bar down, making sure the elbows don''t move during the exercise. Without pause go back to the initial position.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','660','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_661','Triceps on Machine','Triceps on Machine','Sit down and hold the bar firmly with your hands. Now press the weight upwards (don''t fully extend your arms) and lower it slowly again. As with other triceps exercises, it''s important not to move your upper arms.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['triceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','661','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_672','Trunk Rotation With Cable','Trunk Rotation With Cable','Seated trunk rotation with cable','BACK',ARRAY['BACK']::text[],ARRAY['lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','672','CC-BY-SA 4','Robertcoop','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_674','Rowing with TRX band','Rowing with TRX band','Rowing with resistance bands - Bodyweight Exercise','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','674','CC-BY-SA 4','Skadi','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_675','Turkish Get-Up','Turkish Get-Up','Starting on back, move to the standing position with dumbbell in one hand.  Switch hands between reps.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','675','CC-BY-SA 4','dookie1481','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_683','Power Clean','Power Clean','Olympic weight lifting','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['chest']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','683','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_684','Underhand Lat Pull Down','Underhand Lat Pull Down','Grip the pull-down bar with your palms facing you and your hands closer than shoulder-width apart. Lean back slightly and keep your back straight. Pull the bar down towards your chest, pulling your shoulders back slightly at the end of the motion.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','684','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_687','Overhead Press','Overhead Press',NULL,'SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','687','CC-BY-SA 4','Vazco','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_688','Upper External Oblique','Upper External Oblique','Exercise for upper external oblique muscles','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['PULL_UP_BAR']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','688','CC-BY-SA 3','http://www.carinatum.com/','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_691','Upright Row, on Multi Press','Upright Row, on Multi Press','The movements are basically the same as with an SZ-bar, but you use the bar on the multi press:

Stand straight, your feet are shoulder-width apart. Hold the bar with an overhand grip on your thighs, the arms are stretched. Lift the bar close to the body till your chin. The elbows point out so that at the highest point they form a V. Make here a short pause before going slowly down and repeating the movement.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps']::text[],'{}'::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_691/0.jpg',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','691','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_693','Upright Row, SZ-bar','Upright Row, SZ-bar','Stand straight, your feet are shoulder-width apart. Hold the SZ-bar with an overhand grip on your thighs, the arms are stretched. Lift the bar close to the body till your chin. The elbows point out so that at the highest point they form a V. Make here a short pause before going slowly down and repeating the movement.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_693/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','693','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_694','Upright Row w/ Dumbbells','Upright Row w/ Dumbbells','Hold a dumbbell in each hand in front of your body. Keep your palms towards your body. Lift you hands straight up until your hands are under your chin, then lower them. Repeat the exercise.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps']::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_694/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','694','CC-BY-SA 4','koreyhinton','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
