('wger_723','Wide-grip Pulldown','Wide-grip Pulldown','Starting position:

Arms extended overhead, feeling a stretch in your lats.
Keep your shoulders depressed (don’t shrug upward).

Pulling phase (concentric):

Pull the bar down to your upper chest or collarbone area by driving your elbows down and back.
Keep your chest lifted and squeeze your shoulder blades together at the bottom.','BACK',ARRAY['BACK','SHOULDERS']::text[],ARRAY['lats','shoulders']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','723','CC-BY-SA 3','tuckerm','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_73','Bench Press','Bench Press','Lay down on a bench, the bar should be directly above your eyes, the knees are somewhat angled and the feet are firmly on the floor. Concentrate, breath deeply and grab the bar more than shoulder wide. Bring it slowly down till it briefly touches your chest at the height of your nipples. Push the bar up.

If you train with a high weight it is advisable to have a spotter that can help you up if you can''t lift the weight on your own.

With the width of the grip you can also control which part of the chest is trained more:

wide grip: outer chest muscles
narrow grip: inner chest muscles and triceps','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_73/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','73','CC-BY-SA 3','sistab2','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_75','Benchpress Dumbbells','Benchpress Dumbbells','Setup and Starting Position: Sit at the end of a flat bench with a dumbbell resting vertically against each thigh. Carefully lean back while driving the dumbbells toward your chest with your knees.

The “Leg Drive” and Posture: Plant your feet firmly on the floor. Retract your shoulder blades (press them together against the bench) and maintain a slight natural lumbar curve.

Starting Position: Push the dumbbells toward the ceiling. Your wrists should be aligned with your elbows. Rotate the dumbbells slightly inward (about 45 degrees) so that your elbows do not splay out too far to the sides, thereby protecting your shoulders.

Eccentric Phase (Lowering): Lower the dumbbells in a controlled manner toward the sides of your chest. Your elbows should lower at an angle of about 45–60 degrees relative to your body. Feel the stretch in the lower part of your chest.

Concentric Phase (Lift): Push the weight upward in a slight arc (toward the center), without letting the dumbbells collide at the top or fully locking out your elbows to maintain muscle tension. Exhale as you lift.

Translated with DeepL.com (free version)','CHEST',ARRAY['CHEST','SHOULDERS','ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['chest','shoulders','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['BENCH','DUMBBELL']::text[],'Chest',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_75/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','75','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_76','Bench Press Narrow Grip','Bench Press Narrow Grip','Setup: Lie flat on the bench and grip the bar at shoulder-width (closer than a standard bench press).
Descent: Lower the bar with control to your lower chest.
Form: Keep your elbows tucked in tight against your torso—do not let them flare out.
Ascent: Press the bar straight back up, squeezing your triceps at the top.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS','SHOULDERS','CHEST']::text[],ARRAY['triceps','shoulders','chest']::text[],ARRAY['BARBELL','BENCH']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_76/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','76','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_79','Bent High Pulls','Bent High Pulls','Bend over slightly while holding two dumbbells.  Pull the dumbbells up to your chest, keeping your elbows as high as you can.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],ARRAY['DUMBBELL']::text[],'Shoulders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_79/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','79','CC-BY-SA 3','lakerbeezel','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
