('wger_94','Biceps Curls With SZ-bar','Biceps Curls With SZ-bar','Hold the SZ-bar shoulder-wide, the back is straight, the shoulders slightly back, the arms are streched. Bend the arms, bringing the weight up, with a fast movement. Without pausing, let down the bar with a slow and controlled movement.

Don''t allow your body to swing during the exercise, all work is done by the biceps, which are the only mucles that should move (pay attention to the elbows).','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_94/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','94','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_95','Biceps Curl With Cable','Biceps Curl With Cable','Stand around 30 - 40cm away from the cable, the feet are firmly on the floor. Take the bar and lift the weight with a fast movements. Lower the weight as with the dumbbell curls slowly and controlled.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_95/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','95','CC-BY-SA 3','wger.de','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_957','Quadriped Arm and Leg Raise','Quadriped Arm and Leg Raise','In this exercise, the back muscles and the muscles of the back of the leg and back of the arm are activated by lifting the crossed arm and leg at the same time in the crawling position. It also improves balance and proprioception. The movement is done symmetrically.

Get into a crawling posture.2. Draw your abdomen in, then raise your right leg and left arm.3. You should keep your abdomen in for 8 seconds.4. After 8 seconds, slowly lower your arm and leg.5. Then release your muscle.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_957/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','957','CC-BY-SA 4','utkb','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_958','Biceps with TRX','Biceps with TRX','Grab the handles of the TRX straps, lean your body back, arms and legs extended, with your body positioned in a single straight line. (This is an arm exercise, not an abdominal one.)','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_958/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','958','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_959','TRX Rows','TRX Rows','This exercise serves as a lead-up to Pull Ups.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','ARMS','BACK']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','biceps','lats']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Back',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_959/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','959','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_960','Kettlebell Swing','Kettlebell Swing','While kettlebell swings are a full-body workout, they mostly target the muscles along the posterior chain (back of the body). The main muscles used are the glutes, hamstrings, spinal erectors, and muscles of the upper back.','SHOULDERS',ARRAY['SHOULDERS','LEGS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['shoulders','glutes','quads','core']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_960/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','960','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_961','Swimming 50m sprints','Swimming 50m sprints','50m swimming sprints at 1min','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],'{}'::text[],'{}'::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','961','CC-BY-SA 4','abuono','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_962','Elliptical','Elliptical','It improves muscle toning, strengthens the leg muscles (quads, glutes, calves), helps vascularisation and increases resistance. The elliptical is also very useful if you aim to lose weight. Teste','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS','ARMS','CORE']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads','biceps','core','triceps']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Cardio',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','962','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_974','Curl with kettlebell two hands','Curl with kettlebell two hands','Stand upright and grip the kettlebell with both hands. Perform the elbow flexion motion, starting from a fully extended position until your hand reaches shoulder height. Spread your legs a little for stability and, to perform the exercise correctly, try not to push with your back or body in general. Change the weight of the kettlebell to adjust the difficulty.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],NULL,FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','974','CC-BY-SA 4',NULL,'https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_975','one-handed kettlebell curls','one-handed kettlebell curls','Standing with the kettlebell in one hand and bent at the elbow, start from a fully extended position until your hand reaches shoulder height. To perform the movement correctly, try not to push with your back or body.','ARMS',ARRAY['ARMS']::text[],ARRAY['biceps']::text[],ARRAY['KETTLEBELL']::text[],'Arms',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_975/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','975','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_976','Medicine ball booklet crunch','Medicine ball booklet crunch','Using a medicine ball as an overload will make the exercise heavier.','CORE',ARRAY['CORE']::text[],ARRAY['core']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Abs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_976/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','976','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
('wger_977','Box squat','Box squat','Set up the box: Position the box behind you, about 3 feet from a squat rack if you''re using a barbell. Choose a height that allows you to squat down and gently tap your glutes on the box with your back straight.
Stand with proper form: Stand with your feet shoulder-width apart, toes pointed slightly outward. Engage your core and keep your back neutral. If using a barbell, rack it at shoulder height.
Lower down: Sit back as if going to sit on a chair, bending your knees and lowering your hips towards the box. Keep your core tight and back straight throughout the movement.
Controlled descent: Descend in a controlled manner until your glutes gently touch the box. Don''t plop down.
Pause and press up: Briefly pause at the bottom with your back straight and core engaged. Then, press through your heels to drive yourself back up to the starting position.

Improvements in coordination, balance and endurance, toning of the leg and buttock muscles and an overall increase in bone density eliminating the risk of osteoporosis.','LEGS',ARRAY['LEGS']::text[],ARRAY['glutes','quads']::text[],ARRAY['OTHER']::text[],'Legs',NULL,NULL,NULL,'EITHER',NULL,0,'{}'::text[],'https://ilzlswmatadlnsuxatcv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/exercise-media/wger_977/0.png',FALSE,FALSE,NULL,'wger','977','CC-BY-SA 4','clafal','https://wger.de/en/software/api'),
